{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794830066500,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","part":{"id":"prt_1e4356344001FN482nJ4liVJvS","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","messageID":"msg_1e4355598001SxMH8nQ4vBrBbc","type":"step-start","snapshot":"10f40a084ec49a35ccbd03fd868c40f7f31d93b0"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830067135,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4356401002HBWSBfcRD0eePR","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","messageID":"msg_1e4355598001SxMH8nQ4vBrBbc","type":"tool","id":"call_0376bc165b754c43b2200dae","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":330,"offset":925,"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 925-1254\n925:           - convergence_mode: \"Extract antiConvergence.convergenceMode when it is one of 'default', 'off', 'sliding-window', or 'divergent'; default to 'default'\"\n926:           - convergence_mode_warning: \"Boolean true when antiConvergence.convergenceMode is present with an unsupported value; use 'default'\"\n927:           - pivot_lineage: \"Summarize registry.divergence.completed and registry.divergence.overrides with pivot ids, source iterations, and selected review direction; else 'none yet'\"\n928:           - saturated_directions: \"List registry.divergence.saturatedDirections; else 'none yet'\"\n929:           - review_focus_block: \"When deep-review-config.json reviewFocus is a non-empty string, return 'Operator review focus (cover it in addition to the dimension of this iteration, and say in the narrative how you addressed it): <reviewFocus>'. Else return an empty string.\"\n930:           - unfinished_core_protocols_block: \"Under the same condition as next_dimension's traceability case, return 'This is the last iteration under the cap. Finish these core traceability protocols: <ids, comma-separated>. Record one traceabilityChecks.results[] entry for each. A result raised from partial to pass needs a file:line reference in evidenceRefs, or it stays partial.' Else return an empty string.\"\n931: \n932:       step_check_max_duration:\n933:         action: \"Stop the loop when the run has used its wall-clock budget, and still synthesize\"\n934:         command: |\n935:           node -e '\n936:             const config = JSON.parse(require(\"fs\").readFileSync(process.argv[1], \"utf8\"));\n937:             const maxDurationMinutes = Number(config.maxDurationMinutes);\n938:             const startedMs = Date.parse(config.createdAt);\n939:             const elapsedMinutes = Math.floor((Date.now() - startedMs) / 60000);\n940:             const reached = Number.isFinite(maxDurationMinutes) && maxDurationMinutes > 0\n941:               && Number.isFinite(startedMs) && elapsedMinutes >= maxDurationMinutes;\n942:             console.log(JSON.stringify({ elapsedMinutes, maxDurationMinutes, reached }));\n943:           ' \"{state_paths.config}\"\n944:         outputs:\n945:           - duration_reached: \"reached from the JSON output\"\n946:           - elapsed_minutes: \"elapsedMinutes from the JSON output\"\n947:         note: \"The clock starts at the createdAt of the current generation's config. A resume keeps it and a restart resets it, so paused and waiting time counts.\"\n948:         if_reached:\n949:           when: \"duration_reached == true\"\n950:           set: { decision: \"STOP\", reason: \"maxDurationReached\", stopReason: \"maxDurationReached\" }\n951:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"maxDurationReached\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"maxDurationReached\",\"elapsedMinutes\":{elapsed_minutes},\"maxDurationMinutes\":{config.maxDurationMinutes},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n952:           log: \"Duration limit reached after {elapsed_minutes} minutes. Skipping dispatch and entering synthesis with partial findings.\"\n953:           run_first: record_terminal_gates\n954:           skip_to: phase_synthesis\n955:           note: \"The stop row is printed, not appended: the gateway refuses an event it has no ledger stem for. The reason reaches the synthesis report through the bound reason.\"\n956:         if_not_reached:\n957:           action: \"Continue with the iteration\"\n958: \n959:       step_check_pause_sentinel:\n960:         action: \"Check for pause sentinel file\"\n961:         check: \"Does {state_paths.pause_sentinel} exist?\"\n962:         if_exists:\n963:           set:\n964:             pending_stop_event: \"paused\"\n965:             pending_stop_reason: \"userPaused\"\n966:             pending_stop_detail: \"sentinel file detected\"\n967:           skip_to: step_normalize_pause_events\n968:         if_not_exists:\n969:           proceed: true\n970: \n971:       step_validate_convergence_config:\n972:         action: \"Validate convergence mode when loading config\"\n973:         if_convergence_mode_invalid:\n974:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"field\":\"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\",\"fallback\":\"default\",\"message\":\"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n975:           dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n976:           log: \"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\"\n977: \n978:       step_graph_convergence:\n979:         action: \"Run convergence.cjs once: it evaluates the coverage graph and computes the whole review stop decision\"\n980:         inspect:\n981:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n982:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n983:         transform: |\n984:           1. Call convergence.cjs once on the current review lineage. It returns the graph decision and the stop_decision object.\n985:           2. Record the decision as one of CONTINUE, STOP_ALLOWED, STOP_BLOCKED.\n986:           3. Preserve raw graph signals and blockers for reducer rollup and blocked-stop evidence.\n987:           4. Normalize blockers to both JSON array and CSV forms for downstream stop handling.\n988:           5. Set graph_stop_blocked = true only when graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\".\n989:         bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"review\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\" --stop-decision --config-path \"{state_paths.config}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" --iteration-count \"{iteration_count}\" --security-sensitive-fix-scope \"{security_sensitive_fix_scope}\" --fix-replay-required-rows \"{fix_completeness_replay_required_rows}\" --fix-replay-passing-rows \"{fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows}\"'\n990:         note: \"The script is the only place the stop decision is computed. step_check_convergence branches on its stop_decision output.\"\n991:         append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.graph_convergence_evaluated\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"rawSignals\":{graph_raw_signals_json},\"weightedSignals\":{graph_raw_signals_json},\"dimensionCoverageDigest\":\"{dimension_coverage_digest}\",\"protocolCoverageDigest\":\"{protocol_coverage_digest}\",\"findingStability\":\"{finding_stability}\",\"p0p1ResolutionState\":\"{p0p1_resolution_state}\",\"evidenceDensity\":{evidence_density},\"hotspotSaturation\":{hotspot_saturation},\"decision\":\"{graph_decision_code}\",\"policyFingerprint\":\"{policy_fingerprint}\",\"blockerIds\":{graph_blocker_ids_json},\"stopCandidate\":{stop_candidate},\"graphDecision\":\"{graph_decision_code}\",\"graphDigest\":\"{graph_digest}\",\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json}},\"eventId\":\"graph-{session_id}-g{generation}-i{current_iteration}\"}'\n992:         dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n993:         on_missing_counters: \"If loop_counters_json is missing from the output, halt with stop reason error. Never bind a default counter. Run step_release_lock before the halt returns control.\"\n994:         outputs:\n995:           - graph_decision: \"CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED\"\n996:           - stop_decision: \"Tool stop_decision object: decision, stopReason, reasonDetail, weightedStopScore, signals, gates, blockedBy, graphDecision, inputs\"\n997:           - loop_counters_json: \"Tool loop_counters_json object: stuckCount and consecutiveFailureCount, both rebuilt from the state log on this pass\"\n998:           - stuck_count: \"loop_counters_json.stuckCount\"\n999:           - consecutive_failure_count: \"loop_counters_json.consecutiveFailureCount\"\n1000:           - graph_decision_code: \"CONTINUE maps to continue, STOP_ALLOWED to converged, STOP_BLOCKED to blocked\"\n1001:           - graph_signals_json: \"JSON object returned by convergence.cjs\"\n1002:           - graph_raw_signals_json: \"Exact-field convergence-signals JSON built from the convergence.cjs signals; observationDigest is the sha256 of graph_signals_json\"\n1003:           - graph_blockers_json: \"JSON array of graph blockers when present, else []\"\n1004:           - graph_blocker_ids_json: \"JSON array of blocker type values; use [\\\"graph_blocker\\\"] when the decision is blocked and the list is empty\"\n1005:           - graph_blockers_csv: \"Comma-separated blocker summary when graph blocks STOP, else empty string\"\n1006:           - graph_stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n1007:           - dimension_coverage_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON of the registry dimensionCoverage map\"\n1008:           - protocol_coverage_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON of the protocol coverage object in graph_signals_json, or of {} when absent\"\n1009:           - finding_stability: \"stable when findingStabilityRatio >= convergenceThreshold, unstable when below, unknown when the signal is missing\"\n1010:           - p0p1_resolution_state: \"resolved when active P0 + P1 findings are 0, blocked when above 0, unknown when counts are unavailable\"\n1011:           - evidence_density: \"evidenceDensityRatio from graph_signals_json, capped at 1\"\n1012:           - hotspot_saturation: \"hotspotSaturationRatio from graph_signals_json, between 0 and 1\"\n1013:           - policy_fingerprint: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON {convergenceThreshold, stopPolicy, convergenceMode} from the review config\"\n1014:           - stop_candidate: \"true when graph_decision == STOP_ALLOWED, else false\"\n1015:           - graph_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of graph_signals_json\"\n1016: \n1017:       step_check_convergence:\n1018:         action: \"Branch on the stop decision that convergence.cjs computed in step_graph_convergence\"\n1019:         algorithm: |\n1020:           The whole stop decision is computed by convergence.cjs from the review config, the state log, the findings registry and the coverage graph. This step performs no arithmetic and never recomputes or overrides the result.\n1021:           The ratio signals leave out thought iterations and every iteration whose status is error or timeout, and stuck_count is loop_counters_json.stuckCount.\n1022:           The script applies this fixed order, first match wins:\n1023:           1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap is evaluated before every veto, the claim-adjudication veto included; failed legal-stop gates are recorded in stop_decision.blockedBy as synthesis evidence.\n1024:           1a. After 3 consecutive failed iterations (status error or timeout), halt the loop and enter synthesis with stop reason error and partial findings.\n1025:           2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n1026:           3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue.\n1027:           3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: the vote is telemetry only and the decision is CONTINUE.\n1028:           4. a STOP candidate exists when every dimension is clean (all_dimensions_clean) or the weighted vote passes (composite_converged). The vote cutoffs follow the configured convergenceThreshold.\n1029:           5. the nine legal-stop gates run on a candidate: convergenceGate, dimensionCoverageGate, p0ResolutionGate, evidenceDensityGate, hotspotSaturationGate, claimAdjudicationGate, fixCompletenessReplayGate, candidateCoverageGate, graphlessFallbackGate. Any failed gate gives BLOCKED (blockedStop).\n1030:           6. the graph decision settles the candidate: STOP_ALLOWED keeps STOP, STOP_BLOCKED gives BLOCKED, CONTINUE or a missing graph decision gives CONTINUE.\n1031:           Bind the outputs from stop_decision, where G is stop_decision.gates and I is stop_decision.inputs.review:\n1032:             decision = stop_decision.decision\n1033:             stopReason = stop_decision.stopReason\n1034:             reason = stop_decision.stopReason when it is not null, else stop_decision.reasonDetail\n1035:             reason_detail = stop_decision.reasonDetail\n1036:             weighted_stop_score = stop_decision.weightedStopScore\n1037:             stop_blocked = (stop_decision.decision == \"BLOCKED\")\n1038:             blocked_by_json = stop_decision.blockedBy\n1039:             blocked_by_csv = the members of stop_decision.blockedBy joined with commas\n1040:             convergence_gate_pass = G.convergenceGate.pass\n1041:             convergence_gate_score = G.convergenceGate.score\n1042:             dimension_coverage_gate_pass = G.dimensionCoverageGate.pass\n1043:             dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json = G.dimensionCoverageGate.missing\n1044:             dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json = the configured review dimensions that are not in G.dimensionCoverageGate.missing\n1045:             p0_resolution_gate_pass = G.p0ResolutionGate.pass\n1046:             active_p0_count = G.p0ResolutionGate.activeP0\n1047:             evidence_density_gate_pass = G.evidenceDensityGate.pass\n1048:             avg_evidence_per_finding = I.evidenceBackedP0P1, the count of active P0 and P1 findings that carry file:line evidence\n1049:             hotspot_saturation_gate_pass = G.hotspotSaturationGate.pass\n1050:             claim_adjudication_gate_pass = G.claimAdjudicationGate.pass\n1051:             claim_adjudication_active_count = I.activeP0 plus I.activeP1\n1052:             fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass = G.fixCompletenessReplayGate.pass\n1053:             security_sensitive_fix_scope = I.securitySensitiveFixScope\n1054:             fix_completeness_replay_required_rows = I.fixReplayRequiredRows\n1055:             fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows = I.fixReplayPassingRows\n1056:             candidate_coverage_gate_pass = G.candidateCoverageGate.pass\n1057:             candidate_coverage_search_debt_json = I.searchDebt\n1058:             candidate_coverage_missing_json = the I.requiredBugClasses entries that are not in I.candidateCovered\n1059:             graphless_fallback_gate_pass = G.graphlessFallbackGate.pass\n1060:             graphless_fallback_mode = I.graphCoverageMode\n1061:             graphless_fallback_missing_json = the I.requiredBugClasses entries that are not in I.fallbackCoveredBugClasses\n1062:             graphless_fallback_unavailability_reason = the explicit reason when I.graphCoverageMode == \"unavailable_blocked\", else empty string\n1063:             graph_blocker_detail_json = graph_blockers_json\n1064:             recovery_strategy = one line naming the next review action for the gates in stop_decision.blockedBy. When claimAdjudicationGate is listed: \"Reviewer must add typed claim-adjudication packets (claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger) for every active P0/P1 finding before STOP is allowed.\" When stop_decision.reasonDetail == \"graphStopBlocked\": \"Resolve review coverage-graph blockers before stopping.\" When candidateCoverageGate and graphlessFallbackGate both fail, combine their guidance. When I.unfinishedCoreProtocols is non-empty, name them and say the last iteration under the cap is reserved for them, each needing file:line evidence.\n1065:           If stop_decision is missing from the step_graph_convergence output, do not decide by hand: halt and report the script output.\n1066:         outputs:\n1067:           - decision: \"STOP | BLOCKED | STUCK_RECOVERY | CONTINUE\"\n1068:           - reason: \"stop_decision.stopReason when set, else stop_decision.reasonDetail\"\n1069:           - reason_detail: \"stop_decision.reasonDetail, the fine cause behind the decision\"\n1070:           - weighted_stop_score: \"stop_decision.weightedStopScore, for diagnostics only\"\n1071:           - stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when STOP is vetoed by inline legal-stop gates or graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n1072:           - blocked_by_json: \"JSON array of failed legal-stop gates when decision == BLOCKED\"\n1073:           - blocked_by_csv: \"Comma-separated list of failed legal-stop gates when decision == BLOCKED\"\n1074:           - convergence_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for convergenceGate\"\n1075:           - convergence_gate_score: \"Numeric score recorded for convergenceGate\"\n1076:           - dimension_coverage_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for dimensionCoverageGate\"\n1077:           - dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json: \"JSON array of covered review dimensions\"\n1078:           - dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json: \"JSON array of missing review dimensions\"\n1079:           - p0_resolution_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for p0ResolutionGate\"\n1080:           - active_p0_count: \"Active P0 finding count at stop-check time\"\n1081:           - evidence_density_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for evidenceDensityGate\"\n1082:           - avg_evidence_per_finding: \"Numeric evidence density for active findings\"\n1083:           - hotspot_saturation_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for hotspotSaturationGate\"\n1084:           - claim_adjudication_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for claimAdjudicationGate (false vetoes STOP)\"\n1085:           - claim_adjudication_active_count: \"Count of active P0/P1 findings evaluated by claimAdjudicationGate\"\n1086:           - fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for fixCompletenessReplayGate (false vetoes STOP on security-sensitive fix reruns)\"\n1087:           - security_sensitive_fix_scope: \"Boolean true when the review is a security-sensitive fix rerun\"\n1088:           - fix_completeness_replay_required_rows: \"Count of closed-gate replay rows required before STOP\"\n1089:           - fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows: \"Count of required closed-gate replay rows that passed with evidence\"\n1090:           - candidate_coverage_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for candidateCoverageGate (false vetoes STOP for unresolved reducer-owned search debt or uncovered required bug classes)\"\n1091:           - candidate_coverage_search_debt_json: \"JSON array of reducer-owned searchDebt obligations used as blocked-stop evidence\"\n1092:           - candidate_coverage_missing_json: \"JSON array of required bug classes missing from candidateCoverage.covered\"\n1093:           - graphless_fallback_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for graphlessFallbackGate (false vetoes STOP when graphless fallback evidence is absent or unavailable_blocked)\"\n1094:           - graphless_fallback_mode: \"Latest reducer-owned searchCoverage.graphCoverageMode value\"\n1095:           - graphless_fallback_missing_json: \"JSON array of required bug classes missing cited fallback ledger rows\"\n1096:           - graphless_fallback_unavailability_reason: \"Explicit unavailability reason when graphCoverageMode == unavailable_blocked\"\n1097:           - graph_decision: \"CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED from step_graph_convergence\"\n1098:           - graph_signals_json: \"JSON object returned by graph convergence\"\n1099:           - graph_blockers_json: \"JSON array of graph blockers\"\n1100:           - graph_blockers_csv: \"Comma-separated graph blocker summary\"\n1101:           - recovery_strategy: \"One-line hint describing the next review action when decision == BLOCKED or STUCK_RECOVERY\"\n1102:           - recovery_strategy_code: \"Slug form of recovery_strategy for the ledger code fields\"\n1103:           - gate_results_array_json: \"One {gateId,status,reasonCode,evidenceDigest} row per legal-stop gate (convergenceGate, dimensionCoverageGate, evidenceDensityGate, hotspotSaturationGate, claimAdjudicationGate, fixCompletenessReplayGate, candidateCoverageGate, graphlessFallbackGate), with at least one fail row when decision == BLOCKED\"\n1104:           - active_total_count: \"p0_count + p1_count + p2_count, the active findings total\"\n1105: \n1106:       step_emit_blocked_stop:\n1107:         action: \"Persist blocked-stop evidence whenever the review legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP\"\n1108:         if_blocked:\n1109:           append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.blocked_stop_recorded\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"blockedGateIds\":{blocked_by_json},\"gateResults\":{gate_results_array_json},\"activeFindingCounts\":{\"candidates\":{active_total_count},\"adjudicated\":{active_total_count},\"p0\":{p0_count},\"p1\":{p1_count},\"p2\":{p2_count}},\"recoveryStrategy\":\"{recovery_strategy_code}\",\"targetDimensionId\":\"{next_dimension}\",\"originatingConvergenceEventId\":\"graph-{session_id}-g{generation}-i{current_iteration}\",\"appendPosition\":{current_iteration},\"gateDetail\":{gate_results_array_json},\"graphBlockerDetail\":{graph_blockers_json},\"recoveryHint\":\"{recovery_strategy}\"}}'\n1110:           dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n1111:           log: \"Blocked STOP persisted for review loop. Failed gates: {blocked_by_csv}. Recovery strategy: {recovery_strategy}\"\n1112:         if_not_blocked:\n1113:           proceed: true\n1114: \n1115:       step_handle_convergence:\n1116:         action: \"Act on convergence decision\"\n1117:         if_consecutive_failures:\n1118:           applies_to: confirm\n1119:           when: \"stop_decision.reasonDetail == 'consecutiveFailures'. This branch runs instead of if_stop.\"\n1120:           gate_consecutive_failures:\n1121:             type: approval_gate\n1122:             purpose: \"In confirm mode, ask the operator Retry / Skip / Cancel before synthesis starts.\"\n1123:             present: |\n1124:               **{consecutive_failure_count} iterations in a row failed.**\n1125: \n1126:               Options:\n1127:               A) Retry: dispatch the next iteration with the same dimension\n1128:               B) Skip: dispatch the next iteration with the next dimension\n1129:               C) Cancel: end the run with no synthesis\n1130:             wait_for: \"User response\"\n1131:             after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1132:             on_A: { set: { decision: \"CONTINUE\" }, proceed_to: step_normalize_pause_events }\n1133:             on_B: { action: \"Advance next_dimension to the next uncovered dimension in strategy.md\", set: { decision: \"CONTINUE\" }, proceed_to: step_normalize_pause_events }\n1134:             on_C: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n1135:           note: \"The failure count is rebuilt from the state log, so this gate asks again after each further failed iteration and stops asking once an iteration completes.\"\n1136:         if_stop:\n1137:           record_terminal_gates:\n1138:             when: \"Run once, immediately before control jumps to phase_synthesis: in if_existing_terminal_path, in the divergent pivot's if_failed and on_error branches, and in every confirm-mode manualStop exit (on_C) into phase_synthesis: both divergent pivot gates, gate_pre_iteration and the post-iteration gate. The auto three-errors stop (reason error) reaches it through if_existing_terminal_path. The duration stop in step_check_max_duration runs it, once, before its jump to phase_synthesis. Never run it when the pivot continues the loop.\"\n1139:             bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/terminal-gates.cjs --config-path \"{state_paths.config}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"'\n1140:             note: \"The script computes all three gates from the config, state log and registry: evidence by the evidenceDensityGate rule, coverage by the dimensionCoverageGate rule, and scope by matching every open finding's file against reviewScopeFiles. Never judge a gate from the findings yourself. Run it fresh at this stop, even when an earlier blocked stop recorded failures.\"\n1141:             on_error: \"When the script exits non-zero or prints status error, fail closed: bind terminal_gate_results_json to three rows, evidence, scope and coverage, each with status fail, reasonCode gate-script-error and evidenceDigest the sha256 of the script's error text, and bind failed_required_gate_ids to [\\\"evidence\\\",\\\"scope\\\",\\\"coverage\\\"].\"\n1142:             evaluate: |\n1143:               terminal_stop_reason = reason when it is maxIterationsReached, maxDurationReached, manualStop or error, else \"converged\". Read reason, never stopReason: every manual stop sets reason to manualStop while stopReason may still hold blockedStop or stuckRecovery\n1144:             outputs:\n1145:               - terminal_gate_results_json: \"Tool terminal_gate_results_json: three rows {gateId, status, reasonCode, evidenceDigest} in the order evidence, scope, coverage\"\n1146:               - failed_required_gate_ids: \"Tool failed_required_gate_ids: the gateIds whose status is fail, in that order; [] when all pass\"\n1147:               - terminal_stop_reason: \"From evaluate\"\n1148:             append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.terminal_gates_recorded\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"stopReason\":\"{terminal_stop_reason}\",\"gateResults\":{terminal_gate_results_json},\"failedRequiredGateIds\":{failed_required_gate_ids},\"appendPosition\":{current_iteration}}}'\n1149:             log: \"Terminal gates recorded at stop {terminal_stop_reason}. Failed required gates: {failed_required_gate_ids}\"\n1150:           branch_on: \"convergence_mode == 'divergent' AND stop_decision.reasonDetail == 'all_dimensions_clean'\"\n1151:           if_divergent_eligible:\n1152:             eligibility_contract:\n1153:               required_decision: \"STOP\"\n1154:               eligible_reasons: [all_dimensions_clean]\n1155:               excluded_reasons: [maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused, maxDurationReached]\n1156:               fail_closed: \"Any missing or ambiguous reason uses if_existing_terminal_path without preparing a pivot. The nine legal-stop gates have already run and remain unchanged.\"\n1157:             steps:\n1158:               step_prepare_divergent_pivot:\n1159:                 action: \"Generate state-grounded read-only review candidates and prepare or resume the pivot transaction\"\n1160:                 dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1161:                 command: |\n1162:                   node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs prepare --loop-type review --artifact-root \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" --config \"{state_paths.config}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --strategy \"{state_paths.strategy}\" --registry \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" --current-iteration \"{current_iteration}\" --max-iterations \"{max_iterations}\" --trigger-reason \"{reason_detail}\"\n1163:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1164:                 outputs:\n1165:                   - pivot_prepare_json: \"The complete parsed JSON result\"\n1166:                   - pivot_prepare_status: \"status from the prepare result\"\n1167:                   - pivot_id: \"pivotId from the prepare result\"\n1168:                   - pivot_paths_json: \"paths from the prepare result as JSON\"\n1169:                   - pivot_resumed: \"resumed from the prepare result\"\n1170:                   - pivot_missing_seat_ids: \"missingSeats ids from a pending result\"\n1171:                   - pivot_seat_json: \"For the current seat_id, its mandate object from missingSeats\"\n1172:                   - pivot_seat_prompt: \"For the current seat_id, seatPrompts[seat_id]\"\n1173:                   - pivot_dispatch_context_json: \"dispatchContext from a pending result as JSON\"\n1174:                 short_circuit: \"When status is completed or failed, skip all dispatch and record steps and bind this result as pivot_result.\"\n1175: \n1176:               step_dispatch_pivot_seat:\n1177:                 action: \"Natively dispatch one read-only review direction-selection seat\"\n1178:                 for_each: \"seat_id in [seat-001, seat-002, seat-003], in that order. Run this step and then step_record_pivot_seat for one seat before the next seat starts. Seat roles: seat-001 analytical, seat-002 critical, seat-003 pragmatic.\"\n1179:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain seat_id\"\n1180:                 dry_run_boundary: \"dispatch\"\n1181:                 capture_timing: true\n1182:                 if_native:\n1183:                   dispatch:\n1184:                     agent: deep-review\n1185:                     model: opus\n1186:                     context_source: \"pivot_seat_prompt\"\n1187:                   wait_for_completion: true\n1188:                 failure_contract: \"A native dispatch failure binds status=rejected, a {name,message} error, and the measured timestamps/duration, then proceeds to step_record_pivot_seat.\"\n1189:                 outputs:\n1190:                   - pivot_seat_dispatch_status: \"fulfilled or rejected\"\n1191:                   - pivot_seat_output_json: \"Raw native return serialized as JSON when fulfilled, else null\"\n1192:                   - pivot_seat_error_json: \"{name,message} when rejected, else null\"\n1193:                   - pivot_seat_started_at_iso: \"Dispatch start timestamp\"\n1194:                   - pivot_seat_completed_at_iso: \"Dispatch completion timestamp\"\n1195:                   - pivot_seat_duration_ms: \"Dispatch duration in milliseconds\"\n1196: \n1197:               step_record_pivot_seat:\n1198:                 action: \"Durably record the native dispatch outcome of the seat just dispatched\"\n1199:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain seat_id\"\n1200:                 command: |\n1201:                   node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs record-seat <<'PIVOT_SEAT'\n1202:                   {\"paths\":{pivot_paths_json},\"pivotId\":\"{pivot_id}\",\"seat\":{pivot_seat_json},\"status\":\"{pivot_seat_dispatch_status}\",\"output\":{pivot_seat_output_json},\"error\":{pivot_seat_error_json},\"startedAtIso\":\"{pivot_seat_started_at_iso}\",\"completedAtIso\":\"{pivot_seat_completed_at_iso}\",\"durationMs\":\"{pivot_seat_duration_ms}\"}\n1203:                   PIVOT_SEAT\n1204:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1205: \n1206:               step_finalize_divergent_pivot:\n1207:                 action: \"Finalize the prepared pivot after all missing native seats are durable\"\n1208:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending'\"\n1209:                 command: |\n1210:                   node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs finalize --paths-json '{pivot_paths_json}' --pivot-id \"{pivot_id}\" --resumed \"{pivot_resumed}\"\n1211:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1212:                 outputs:\n1213:                   - pivot_finalize_json: \"The complete parsed final result\"\n1214: \n1215:               step_resolve_divergent_pivot_result:\n1216:                 action: \"Use prepare's terminal result on resume/short-circuit, otherwise use finalize's result\"\n1217:                 branch_on: \"pivot_prepare_status\"\n1218:                 if_pending: { bind: { pivot_result: \"{pivot_finalize_json}\" } }\n1219:                 if_completed_or_failed: { bind: { pivot_result: \"{pivot_prepare_json}\" } }\n1220: \n1221:               step_apply_divergent_pivot_result:\n1222:                 action: \"Adopt a successful read-only review direction or fail closed to the existing synthesis path\"\n1223:                 branch_on: \"pivot_result.status\"\n1224:                 if_completed:\n1225:                   gate_divergent_pivot_choice:\n1226:                     applies_to: confirm\n1227:                     type: approval_gate\n1228:                     purpose: \"Approve the Council-selected read-only review direction before it becomes the next focus\"\n1229:                     order: \"Under confirm this gate runs before the set, command, log and proceed_to of this branch.\"\n1230:                     present: |\n1231:                       ## Divergent Review Pivot Candidate\n1232: \n1233:                       **Pivot**: {pivot_result.pivotId}\n1234:                       **Council-selected candidate**: {pivot_result.selectedCandidate.id}\n1235:                       **Review direction**: {pivot_result.restoredFocus}\n1236:                       **Agreement**: {pivot_result.agreement.endorsementCount}/3 material endorsements\n1237:                       **Swept direction**: {pivot_result.completedEvent.previousFocus}\n1238: \n1239:                       The adapter exposes an ordered candidate frontier and agreement tallies, but no ranked-candidate score contract. Choosing a different ranked candidate is therefore unavailable rather than inferred from array order. Every candidate remains read-only and cannot authorize a fix, target expansion, or file mutation.\n1240: \n1241:                       Options:\n1242:                       A) Accept the Council-selected candidate and continue\n1243:                       B) Choose a different ranked candidate (unavailable: no ranking contract)\n1244:                       C) manualStop and proceed to the existing pre-synthesis gate\n1245:                     wait_for: \"User response\"\n1246:                     after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1247:                     on_A:\n1248:                       bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"pivot_confirm_accepted\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"pivotId\":\"{pivot_result.pivotId}\",\"selectedCandidate\":{pivot_result.selectedCandidate},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n1249:                       continue: \"Run the set, command, log and proceed_to of this branch.\"\n1250:                     on_B:\n1251:                       message: \"No ranked alternative can be selected because the adapter exposes no ranking score or rank contract.\"\n1252:                       return_to: gate_divergent_pivot_choice\n1253:                     on_C:\n1254:                       bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"manualStop\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"manualStop\",\"pivotId\":\"{pivot_result.pivotId}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1255]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 925-1254\n925:           - convergence_mode: \"Extract antiConvergence.convergenceMode when it is one of 'default', 'off', 'sliding-window', or 'divergent'; default to 'default'\"\n926:           - convergence_mode_warning: \"Boolean true when antiConvergence.convergenceMode is present with an unsupported value; use 'default'\"\n927:           - pivot_lineage: \"Summarize registry.divergence.completed and registry.divergence.overrides with pivot ids, source iterations, and selected review direction; else 'none yet'\"\n928:           - saturated_directions: \"List registry.divergence.saturatedDirections; else 'none yet'\"\n929:           - review_focus_block: \"When deep-review-config.json reviewFocus is a non-empty string, return 'Operator review focus (cover it in addition to the dimension of this iteration, and say in the narrative how you addressed it): <reviewFocus>'. Else return an empty string.\"\n930:           - unfinished_core_protocols_block: \"Under the same condition as next_dimension's traceability case, return 'This is the last iteration under the cap. Finish these core traceability protocols: <ids, comma-separated>. Record one traceabilityChecks.results[] entry for each. A result raised from partial to pass needs a file:line reference in evidenceRefs, or it stays partial.' Else return an empty string.\"\n931: \n932:       step_check_max_duration:\n933:         action: \"Stop the loop when the run has used its wall-clock budget, and still synthesize\"\n934:         command: |\n935:           node -e '\n936:             const config = JSON.parse(require(\"fs\").readFileSync(process.argv[1], \"utf8\"));\n937:             const maxDurationMinutes = Number(config.maxDurationMinutes);\n938:             const startedMs = Date.parse(config.createdAt);\n939:             const elapsedMinutes = Math.floor((Date.now() - startedMs) / 60000);\n940:             const reached = Number.isFinite(maxDurationMinutes) && maxDurationMinutes > 0\n941:               && Number.isFinite(startedMs) && elapsedMinutes >= maxDurationMinutes;\n942:             console.log(JSON.stringify({ elapsedMinutes, maxDurationMinutes, reached }));\n943:           ' \"{state_paths.config}\"\n944:         outputs:\n945:           - duration_reached: \"reached from the JSON output\"\n946:           - elapsed_minutes: \"elapsedMinutes from the JSON output\"\n947:         note: \"The clock starts at the createdAt of the current generation's config. A resume keeps it and a restart resets it, so paused and waiting time counts.\"\n948:         if_reached:\n949:           when: \"duration_reached == true\"\n950:           set: { decision: \"STOP\", reason: \"maxDurationReached\", stopReason: \"maxDurationReached\" }\n951:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"maxDurationReached\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"maxDurationReached\",\"elapsedMinutes\":{elapsed_minutes},\"maxDurationMinutes\":{config.maxDurationMinutes},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n952:           log: \"Duration limit reached after {elapsed_minutes} minutes. Skipping dispatch and entering synthesis with partial findings.\"\n953:           run_first: record_terminal_gates\n954:           skip_to: phase_synthesis\n955:           note: \"The stop row is printed, not appended: the gateway refuses an event it has no ledger stem for. The reason reaches the synthesis report through the bound reason.\"\n956:         if_not_reached:\n957:           action: \"Continue with the iteration\"\n958: \n959:       step_check_pause_sentinel:\n960:         action: \"Check for pause sentinel file\"\n961:         check: \"Does {state_paths.pause_sentinel} exist?\"\n962:         if_exists:\n963:           set:\n964:             pending_stop_event: \"paused\"\n965:             pending_stop_reason: \"userPaused\"\n966:             pending_stop_detail: \"sentinel file detected\"\n967:           skip_to: step_normalize_pause_events\n968:         if_not_exists:\n969:           proceed: true\n970: \n971:       step_validate_convergence_config:\n972:         action: \"Validate convergence mode when loading config\"\n973:         if_convergence_mode_invalid:\n974:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"field\":\"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\",\"fallback\":\"default\",\"message\":\"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n975:           dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n976:           log: \"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\"\n977: \n978:       step_graph_convergence:\n979:         action: \"Run convergence.cjs once: it evaluates the coverage graph and computes the whole review stop decision\"\n980:         inspect:\n981:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n982:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n983:         transform: |\n984:           1. Call convergence.cjs once on the current review lineage. It returns the graph decision and the stop_decision object.\n985:           2. Record the decision as one of CONTINUE, STOP_ALLOWED, STOP_BLOCKED.\n986:           3. Preserve raw graph signals and blockers for reducer rollup and blocked-stop evidence.\n987:           4. Normalize blockers to both JSON array and CSV forms for downstream stop handling.\n988:           5. Set graph_stop_blocked = true only when graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\".\n989:         bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"review\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\" --stop-decision --config-path \"{state_paths.config}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" --iteration-count \"{iteration_count}\" --security-sensitive-fix-scope \"{security_sensitive_fix_scope}\" --fix-replay-required-rows \"{fix_completeness_replay_required_rows}\" --fix-replay-passing-rows \"{fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows}\"'\n990:         note: \"The script is the only place the stop decision is computed. step_check_convergence branches on its stop_decision output.\"\n991:         append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.graph_convergence_evaluated\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"rawSignals\":{graph_raw_signals_json},\"weightedSignals\":{graph_raw_signals_json},\"dimensionCoverageDigest\":\"{dimension_coverage_digest}\",\"protocolCoverageDigest\":\"{protocol_coverage_digest}\",\"findingStability\":\"{finding_stability}\",\"p0p1ResolutionState\":\"{p0p1_resolution_state}\",\"evidenceDensity\":{evidence_density},\"hotspotSaturation\":{hotspot_saturation},\"decision\":\"{graph_decision_code}\",\"policyFingerprint\":\"{policy_fingerprint}\",\"blockerIds\":{graph_blocker_ids_json},\"stopCandidate\":{stop_candidate},\"graphDecision\":\"{graph_decision_code}\",\"graphDigest\":\"{graph_digest}\",\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json}},\"eventId\":\"graph-{session_id}-g{generation}-i{current_iteration}\"}'\n992:         dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n993:         on_missing_counters: \"If loop_counters_json is missing from the output, halt with stop reason error. Never bind a default counter. Run step_release_lock before the halt returns control.\"\n994:         outputs:\n995:           - graph_decision: \"CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED\"\n996:           - stop_decision: \"Tool stop_decision object: decision, stopReason, reasonDetail, weightedStopScore, signals, gates, blockedBy, graphDecision, inputs\"\n997:           - loop_counters_json: \"Tool loop_counters_json object: stuckCount and consecutiveFailureCount, both rebuilt from the state log on this pass\"\n998:           - stuck_count: \"loop_counters_json.stuckCount\"\n999:           - consecutive_failure_count: \"loop_counters_json.consecutiveFailureCount\"\n1000:           - graph_decision_code: \"CONTINUE maps to continue, STOP_ALLOWED to converged, STOP_BLOCKED to blocked\"\n1001:           - graph_signals_json: \"JSON object returned by convergence.cjs\"\n1002:           - graph_raw_signals_json: \"Exact-field convergence-signals JSON built from the convergence.cjs signals; observationDigest is the sha256 of graph_signals_json\"\n1003:           - graph_blockers_json: \"JSON array of graph blockers when present, else []\"\n1004:           - graph_blocker_ids_json: \"JSON array of blocker type values; use [\\\"graph_blocker\\\"] when the decision is blocked and the list is empty\"\n1005:           - graph_blockers_csv: \"Comma-separated blocker summary when graph blocks STOP, else empty string\"\n1006:           - graph_stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n1007:           - dimension_coverage_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON of the registry dimensionCoverage map\"\n1008:           - protocol_coverage_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON of the protocol coverage object in graph_signals_json, or of {} when absent\"\n1009:           - finding_stability: \"stable when findingStabilityRatio >= convergenceThreshold, unstable when below, unknown when the signal is missing\"\n1010:           - p0p1_resolution_state: \"resolved when active P0 + P1 findings are 0, blocked when above 0, unknown when counts are unavailable\"\n1011:           - evidence_density: \"evidenceDensityRatio from graph_signals_json, capped at 1\"\n1012:           - hotspot_saturation: \"hotspotSaturationRatio from graph_signals_json, between 0 and 1\"\n1013:           - policy_fingerprint: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON {convergenceThreshold, stopPolicy, convergenceMode} from the review config\"\n1014:           - stop_candidate: \"true when graph_decision == STOP_ALLOWED, else false\"\n1015:           - graph_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of graph_signals_json\"\n1016: \n1017:       step_check_convergence:\n1018:         action: \"Branch on the stop decision that convergence.cjs computed in step_graph_convergence\"\n1019:         algorithm: |\n1020:           The whole stop decision is computed by convergence.cjs from the review config, the state log, the findings registry and the coverage graph. This step performs no arithmetic and never recomputes or overrides the result.\n1021:           The ratio signals leave out thought iterations and every iteration whose status is error or timeout, and stuck_count is loop_counters_json.stuckCount.\n1022:           The script applies this fixed order, first match wins:\n1023:           1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap is evaluated before every veto, the claim-adjudication veto included; failed legal-stop gates are recorded in stop_decision.blockedBy as synthesis evidence.\n1024:           1a. After 3 consecutive failed iterations (status error or timeout), halt the loop and enter synthesis with stop reason error and partial findings.\n1025:           2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n1026:           3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue.\n1027:           3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: the vote is telemetry only and the decision is CONTINUE.\n1028:           4. a STOP candidate exists when every dimension is clean (all_dimensions_clean) or the weighted vote passes (composite_converged). The vote cutoffs follow the configured convergenceThreshold.\n1029:           5. the nine legal-stop gates run on a candidate: convergenceGate, dimensionCoverageGate, p0ResolutionGate, evidenceDensityGate, hotspotSaturationGate, claimAdjudicationGate, fixCompletenessReplayGate, candidateCoverageGate, graphlessFallbackGate. Any failed gate gives BLOCKED (blockedStop).\n1030:           6. the graph decision settles the candidate: STOP_ALLOWED keeps STOP, STOP_BLOCKED gives BLOCKED, CONTINUE or a missing graph decision gives CONTINUE.\n1031:           Bind the outputs from stop_decision, where G is stop_decision.gates and I is stop_decision.inputs.review:\n1032:             decision = stop_decision.decision\n1033:             stopReason = stop_decision.stopReason\n1034:             reason = stop_decision.stopReason when it is not null, else stop_decision.reasonDetail\n1035:             reason_detail = stop_decision.reasonDetail\n1036:             weighted_stop_score = stop_decision.weightedStopScore\n1037:             stop_blocked = (stop_decision.decision == \"BLOCKED\")\n1038:             blocked_by_json = stop_decision.blockedBy\n1039:             blocked_by_csv = the members of stop_decision.blockedBy joined with commas\n1040:             convergence_gate_pass = G.convergenceGate.pass\n1041:             convergence_gate_score = G.convergenceGate.score\n1042:             dimension_coverage_gate_pass = G.dimensionCoverageGate.pass\n1043:             dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json = G.dimensionCoverageGate.missing\n1044:             dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json = the configured review dimensions that are not in G.dimensionCoverageGate.missing\n1045:             p0_resolution_gate_pass = G.p0ResolutionGate.pass\n1046:             active_p0_count = G.p0ResolutionGate.activeP0\n1047:             evidence_density_gate_pass = G.evidenceDensityGate.pass\n1048:             avg_evidence_per_finding = I.evidenceBackedP0P1, the count of active P0 and P1 findings that carry file:line evidence\n1049:             hotspot_saturation_gate_pass = G.hotspotSaturationGate.pass\n1050:             claim_adjudication_gate_pass = G.claimAdjudicationGate.pass\n1051:             claim_adjudication_active_count = I.activeP0 plus I.activeP1\n1052:             fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass = G.fixCompletenessReplayGate.pass\n1053:             security_sensitive_fix_scope = I.securitySensitiveFixScope\n1054:             fix_completeness_replay_required_rows = I.fixReplayRequiredRows\n1055:             fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows = I.fixReplayPassingRows\n1056:             candidate_coverage_gate_pass = G.candidateCoverageGate.pass\n1057:             candidate_coverage_search_debt_json = I.searchDebt\n1058:             candidate_coverage_missing_json = the I.requiredBugClasses entries that are not in I.candidateCovered\n1059:             graphless_fallback_gate_pass = G.graphlessFallbackGate.pass\n1060:             graphless_fallback_mode = I.graphCoverageMode\n1061:             graphless_fallback_missing_json = the I.requiredBugClasses entries that are not in I.fallbackCoveredBugClasses\n1062:             graphless_fallback_unavailability_reason = the explicit reason when I.graphCoverageMode == \"unavailable_blocked\", else empty string\n1063:             graph_blocker_detail_json = graph_blockers_json\n1064:             recovery_strategy = one line naming the next review action for the gates in stop_decision.blockedBy. When claimAdjudicationGate is listed: \"Reviewer must add typed claim-adjudication packets (claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger) for every active P0/P1 finding before STOP is allowed.\" When stop_decision.reasonDetail == \"graphStopBlocked\": \"Resolve review coverage-graph blockers before stopping.\" When candidateCoverageGate and graphlessFallbackGate both fail, combine their guidance. When I.unfinishedCoreProtocols is non-empty, name them and say the last iteration under the cap is reserved for them, each needing file:line evidence.\n1065:           If stop_decision is missing from the step_graph_convergence output, do not decide by hand: halt and report the script output.\n1066:         outputs:\n1067:           - decision: \"STOP | BLOCKED | STUCK_RECOVERY | CONTINUE\"\n1068:           - reason: \"stop_decision.stopReason when set, else stop_decision.reasonDetail\"\n1069:           - reason_detail: \"stop_decision.reasonDetail, the fine cause behind the decision\"\n1070:           - weighted_stop_score: \"stop_decision.weightedStopScore, for diagnostics only\"\n1071:           - stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when STOP is vetoed by inline legal-stop gates or graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n1072:           - blocked_by_json: \"JSON array of failed legal-stop gates when decision == BLOCKED\"\n1073:           - blocked_by_csv: \"Comma-separated list of failed legal-stop gates when decision == BLOCKED\"\n1074:           - convergence_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for convergenceGate\"\n1075:           - convergence_gate_score: \"Numeric score recorded for convergenceGate\"\n1076:           - dimension_coverage_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for dimensionCoverageGate\"\n1077:           - dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json: \"JSON array of covered review dimensions\"\n1078:           - dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json: \"JSON array of missing review dimensions\"\n1079:           - p0_resolution_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for p0ResolutionGate\"\n1080:           - active_p0_count: \"Active P0 finding count at stop-check time\"\n1081:           - evidence_density_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for evidenceDensityGate\"\n1082:           - avg_evidence_per_finding: \"Numeric evidence density for active findings\"\n1083:           - hotspot_saturation_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for hotspotSaturationGate\"\n1084:           - claim_adjudication_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for claimAdjudicationGate (false vetoes STOP)\"\n1085:           - claim_adjudication_active_count: \"Count of active P0/P1 findings evaluated by claimAdjudicationGate\"\n1086:           - fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for fixCompletenessReplayGate (false vetoes STOP on security-sensitive fix reruns)\"\n1087:           - security_sensitive_fix_scope: \"Boolean true when the review is a security-sensitive fix rerun\"\n1088:           - fix_completeness_replay_required_rows: \"Count of closed-gate replay rows required before STOP\"\n1089:           - fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows: \"Count of required closed-gate replay rows that passed with evidence\"\n1090:           - candidate_coverage_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for candidateCoverageGate (false vetoes STOP for unresolved reducer-owned search debt or uncovered required bug classes)\"\n1091:           - candidate_coverage_search_debt_json: \"JSON array of reducer-owned searchDebt obligations used as blocked-stop evidence\"\n1092:           - candidate_coverage_missing_json: \"JSON array of required bug classes missing from candidateCoverage.covered\"\n1093:           - graphless_fallback_gate_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for graphlessFallbackGate (false vetoes STOP when graphless fallback evidence is absent or unavailable_blocked)\"\n1094:           - graphless_fallback_mode: \"Latest reducer-owned searchCoverage.graphCoverageMode value\"\n1095:           - graphless_fallback_missing_json: \"JSON array of required bug classes missing cited fallback ledger rows\"\n1096:           - graphless_fallback_unavailability_reason: \"Explicit unavailability reason when graphCoverageMode == unavailable_blocked\"\n1097:           - graph_decision: \"CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED from step_graph_convergence\"\n1098:           - graph_signals_json: \"JSON object returned by graph convergence\"\n1099:           - graph_blockers_json: \"JSON array of graph blockers\"\n1100:           - graph_blockers_csv: \"Comma-separated graph blocker summary\"\n1101:           - recovery_strategy: \"One-line hint describing the next review action when decision == BLOCKED or STUCK_RECOVERY\"\n1102:           - recovery_strategy_code: \"Slug form of recovery_strategy for the ledger code fields\"\n1103:           - gate_results_array_json: \"One {gateId,status,reasonCode,evidenceDigest} row per legal-stop gate (convergenceGate, dimensionCoverageGate, evidenceDensityGate, hotspotSaturationGate, claimAdjudicationGate, fixCompletenessReplayGate, candidateCoverageGate, graphlessFallbackGate), with at least one fail row when decision == BLOCKED\"\n1104:           - active_total_count: \"p0_count + p1_count + p2_count, the active findings total\"\n1105: \n1106:       step_emit_blocked_stop:\n1107:         action: \"Persist blocked-stop evidence whenever the review legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP\"\n1108:         if_blocked:\n1109:           append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.blocked_stop_recorded\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"blockedGateIds\":{blocked_by_json},\"gateResults\":{gate_results_array_json},\"activeFindingCounts\":{\"candidates\":{active_total_count},\"adjudicated\":{active_total_count},\"p0\":{p0_count},\"p1\":{p1_count},\"p2\":{p2_count}},\"recoveryStrategy\":\"{recovery_strategy_code}\",\"targetDimensionId\":\"{next_dimension}\",\"originatingConvergenceEventId\":\"graph-{session_id}-g{generation}-i{current_iteration}\",\"appendPosition\":{current_iteration},\"gateDetail\":{gate_results_array_json},\"graphBlockerDetail\":{graph_blockers_json},\"recoveryHint\":\"{recovery_strategy}\"}}'\n1110:           dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n1111:           log: \"Blocked STOP persisted for review loop. Failed gates: {blocked_by_csv}. Recovery strategy: {recovery_strategy}\"\n1112:         if_not_blocked:\n1113:           proceed: true\n1114: \n1115:       step_handle_convergence:\n1116:         action: \"Act on convergence decision\"\n1117:         if_consecutive_failures:\n1118:           applies_to: confirm\n1119:           when: \"stop_decision.reasonDetail == 'consecutiveFailures'. This branch runs instead of if_stop.\"\n1120:           gate_consecutive_failures:\n1121:             type: approval_gate\n1122:             purpose: \"In confirm mode, ask the operator Retry / Skip / Cancel before synthesis starts.\"\n1123:             present: |\n1124:               **{consecutive_failure_count} iterations in a row failed.**\n1125: \n1126:               Options:\n1127:               A) Retry: dispatch the next iteration with the same dimension\n1128:               B) Skip: dispatch the next iteration with the next dimension\n1129:               C) Cancel: end the run with no synthesis\n1130:             wait_for: \"User response\"\n1131:             after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1132:             on_A: { set: { decision: \"CONTINUE\" }, proceed_to: step_normalize_pause_events }\n1133:             on_B: { action: \"Advance next_dimension to the next uncovered dimension in strategy.md\", set: { decision: \"CONTINUE\" }, proceed_to: step_normalize_pause_events }\n1134:             on_C: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n1135:           note: \"The failure count is rebuilt from the state log, so this gate asks again after each further failed iteration and stops asking once an iteration completes.\"\n1136:         if_stop:\n1137:           record_terminal_gates:\n1138:             when: \"Run once, immediately before control jumps to phase_synthesis: in if_existing_terminal_path, in the divergent pivot's if_failed and on_error branches, and in every confirm-mode manualStop exit (on_C) into phase_synthesis: both divergent pivot gates, gate_pre_iteration and the post-iteration gate. The auto three-errors stop (reason error) reaches it through if_existing_terminal_path. The duration stop in step_check_max_duration runs it, once, before its jump to phase_synthesis. Never run it when the pivot continues the loop.\"\n1139:             bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/terminal-gates.cjs --config-path \"{state_paths.config}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"'\n1140:             note: \"The script computes all three gates from the config, state log and registry: evidence by the evidenceDensityGate rule, coverage by the dimensionCoverageGate rule, and scope by matching every open finding's file against reviewScopeFiles. Never judge a gate from the findings yourself. Run it fresh at this stop, even when an earlier blocked stop recorded failures.\"\n1141:             on_error: \"When the script exits non-zero or prints status error, fail closed: bind terminal_gate_results_json to three rows, evidence, scope and coverage, each with status fail, reasonCode gate-script-error and evidenceDigest the sha256 of the script's error text, and bind failed_required_gate_ids to [\\\"evidence\\\",\\\"scope\\\",\\\"coverage\\\"].\"\n1142:             evaluate: |\n1143:               terminal_stop_reason = reason when it is maxIterationsReached, maxDurationReached, manualStop or error, else \"converged\". Read reason, never stopReason: every manual stop sets reason to manualStop while stopReason may still hold blockedStop or stuckRecovery\n1144:             outputs:\n1145:               - terminal_gate_results_json: \"Tool terminal_gate_results_json: three rows {gateId, status, reasonCode, evidenceDigest} in the order evidence, scope, coverage\"\n1146:               - failed_required_gate_ids: \"Tool failed_required_gate_ids: the gateIds whose status is fail, in that order; [] when all pass\"\n1147:               - terminal_stop_reason: \"From evaluate\"\n1148:             append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.terminal_gates_recorded\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"stopReason\":\"{terminal_stop_reason}\",\"gateResults\":{terminal_gate_results_json},\"failedRequiredGateIds\":{failed_required_gate_ids},\"appendPosition\":{current_iteration}}}'\n1149:             log: \"Terminal gates recorded at stop {terminal_stop_reason}. Failed required gates: {failed_required_gate_ids}\"\n1150:           branch_on: \"convergence_mode == 'divergent' AND stop_decision.reasonDetail == 'all_dimensions_clean'\"\n1151:           if_divergent_eligible:\n1152:             eligibility_contract:\n1153:               required_decision: \"STOP\"\n1154:               eligible_reasons: [all_dimensions_clean]\n1155:               excluded_reasons: [maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused, maxDurationReached]\n1156:               fail_closed: \"Any missing or ambiguous reason uses if_existing_terminal_path without preparing a pivot. The nine legal-stop gates have already run and remain unchanged.\"\n1157:             steps:\n1158:               step_prepare_divergent_pivot:\n1159:                 action: \"Generate state-grounded read-only review candidates and prepare or resume the pivot transaction\"\n1160:                 dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1161:                 command: |\n1162:                   node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs prepare --loop-type review --artifact-root \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" --config \"{state_paths.config}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --strategy \"{state_paths.strategy}\" --registry \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" --current-iteration \"{current_iteration}\" --max-iterations \"{max_iterations}\" --trigger-reason \"{reason_detail}\"\n1163:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1164:                 outputs:\n1165:                   - pivot_prepare_json: \"The complete parsed JSON result\"\n1166:                   - pivot_prepare_status: \"status from the prepare result\"\n1167:                   - pivot_id: \"pivotId from the prepare result\"\n1168:                   - pivot_paths_json: \"paths from the prepare result as JSON\"\n1169:                   - pivot_resumed: \"resumed from the prepare result\"\n1170:                   - pivot_missing_seat_ids: \"missingSeats ids from a pending result\"\n1171:                   - pivot_seat_json: \"For the current seat_id, its mandate object from missingSeats\"\n1172:                   - pivot_seat_prompt: \"For the current seat_id, seatPrompts[seat_id]\"\n1173:                   - pivot_dispatch_context_json: \"dispatchContext from a pending result as JSON\"\n1174:                 short_circuit: \"When status is completed or failed, skip all dispatch and record steps and bind this result as pivot_result.\"\n1175: \n1176:               step_dispatch_pivot_seat:\n1177:                 action: \"Natively dispatch one read-only review direction-selection seat\"\n1178:                 for_each: \"seat_id in [seat-001, seat-002, seat-003], in that order. Run this step and then step_record_pivot_seat for one seat before the next seat starts. Seat roles: seat-001 analytical, seat-002 critical, seat-003 pragmatic.\"\n1179:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain seat_id\"\n1180:                 dry_run_boundary: \"dispatch\"\n1181:                 capture_timing: true\n1182:                 if_native:\n1183:                   dispatch:\n1184:                     agent: deep-review\n1185:                     model: opus\n1186:                     context_source: \"pivot_seat_prompt\"\n1187:                   wait_for_completion: true\n1188:                 failure_contract: \"A native dispatch failure binds status=rejected, a {name,message} error, and the measured timestamps/duration, then proceeds to step_record_pivot_seat.\"\n1189:                 outputs:\n1190:                   - pivot_seat_dispatch_status: \"fulfilled or rejected\"\n1191:                   - pivot_seat_output_json: \"Raw native return serialized as JSON when fulfilled, else null\"\n1192:                   - pivot_seat_error_json: \"{name,message} when rejected, else null\"\n1193:                   - pivot_seat_started_at_iso: \"Dispatch start timestamp\"\n1194:                   - pivot_seat_completed_at_iso: \"Dispatch completion timestamp\"\n1195:                   - pivot_seat_duration_ms: \"Dispatch duration in milliseconds\"\n1196: \n1197:               step_record_pivot_seat:\n1198:                 action: \"Durably record the native dispatch outcome of the seat just dispatched\"\n1199:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain seat_id\"\n1200:                 command: |\n1201:                   node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs record-seat <<'PIVOT_SEAT'\n1202:                   {\"paths\":{pivot_paths_json},\"pivotId\":\"{pivot_id}\",\"seat\":{pivot_seat_json},\"status\":\"{pivot_seat_dispatch_status}\",\"output\":{pivot_seat_output_json},\"error\":{pivot_seat_error_json},\"startedAtIso\":\"{pivot_seat_started_at_iso}\",\"completedAtIso\":\"{pivot_seat_completed_at_iso}\",\"durationMs\":\"{pivot_seat_duration_ms}\"}\n1203:                   PIVOT_SEAT\n1204:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1205: \n1206:               step_finalize_divergent_pivot:\n1207:                 action: \"Finalize the prepared pivot after all missing native seats are durable\"\n1208:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending'\"\n1209:                 command: |\n1210:                   node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/divergent-pivot.cjs finalize --paths-json '{pivot_paths_json}' --pivot-id \"{pivot_id}\" --resumed \"{pivot_resumed}\"\n1211:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1212:                 outputs:\n1213:                   - pivot_finalize_json: \"The complete parsed final result\"\n1214: \n1215:               step_resolve_divergent_pivot_result:\n1216:                 action: \"Use prepare's terminal result on resume/short-circuit, otherwise use finalize's result\"\n1217:                 branch_on: \"pivot_prepare_status\"\n1218:                 if_pending: { bind: { pivot_result: \"{pivot_finalize_json}\" } }\n1219:                 if_completed_or_failed: { bind: { pivot_result: \"{pivot_prepare_json}\" } }\n1220: \n1221:               step_apply_divergent_pivot_result:\n1222:                 action: \"Adopt a successful read-only review direction or fail closed to the existing synthesis path\"\n1223:                 branch_on: \"pivot_result.status\"\n1224:                 if_completed:\n1225:                   gate_divergent_pivot_choice:\n1226:                     applies_to: confirm\n1227:                     type: approval_gate\n1228:                     purpose: \"Approve the Council-selected read-only review direction before it becomes the next focus\"\n1229:                     order: \"Under confirm this gate runs before the set, command, log and proceed_to of this branch.\"\n1230:                     present: |\n1231:                       ## Divergent Review Pivot Candidate\n1232: \n1233:                       **Pivot**: {pivot_result.pivotId}\n1234:                       **Council-selected candidate**: {pivot_result.selectedCandidate.id}\n1235:                       **Review direction**: {pivot_result.restoredFocus}\n1236:                       **Agreement**: {pivot_result.agreement.endorsementCount}/3 material endorsements\n1237:                       **Swept direction**: {pivot_result.completedEvent.previousFocus}\n1238: \n1239:                       The adapter exposes an ordered candidate frontier and agreement tallies, but no ranked-candidate score contract. Choosing a different ranked candidate is therefore unavailable rather than inferred from array order. Every candidate remains read-only and cannot authorize a fix, target expansion, or file mutation.\n1240: \n1241:                       Options:\n1242:                       A) Accept the Council-selected candidate and continue\n1243:                       B) Choose a different ranked candidate (unavailable: no ranking contract)\n1244:                       C) manualStop and proceed to the existing pre-synthesis gate\n1245:                     wait_for: \"User response\"\n1246:                     after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1247:                     on_A:\n1248:                       bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"pivot_confirm_accepted\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"pivotId\":\"{pivot_result.pivotId}\",\"selectedCandidate\":{pivot_result.selectedCandidate},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n1249:                       continue: \"Run the set, command, log and proceed_to of this branch.\"\n1250:                     on_B:\n1251:                       message: \"No ranked alternative can be selected because the adapter exposes no ranking score or rank contract.\"\n1252:                       return_to: gate_divergent_pivot_choice\n1253:                     on_C:\n1254:                       bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"manualStop\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"manualStop\",\"pivotId\":\"{pivot_result.pivotId}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1255]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":330,\"offset\":925,\"path\":\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830066689,"end":1794830067135}}}}
