{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830078484,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4359208002FmdqLjF06laiof","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","messageID":"msg_1e43588a8001rkRrKbqh4T2vyO","type":"tool","id":"call_f31c7376feba4bd598ff1687","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":330,"offset":1418,"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 1418-1747\n1418:       step_dispatch_iteration:\n1419:         action: \"Dispatch @deep-review agent for one review iteration\"\n1420:         dry_run_boundary: \"dispatch\"\n1421:         dry_run_preview:\n1422:           before_halt:\n1423:             - \"Generate the state summary.\"\n1424:             - \"Render the prompt pack to terminal preview without writing the prompt file.\"\n1425:             - \"Show the selected executor branch and command or native dispatch target that would run.\"\n1426:         pre_dispatch_refresh_lock:\n1427:           action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately before the dispatch starts\"\n1428:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n1429:           on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. Run step_release_lock and stop rather than dispatch without it.\"\n1430:         post_dispatch_refresh_lock:\n1431:           action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately after the dispatch returns\"\n1432:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n1433:           on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. Run step_release_lock and stop rather than continue without it.\"\n1434:         resolve_executor:\n1435:           source: \"config.executor\"\n1436:           loader: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts#parseExecutorConfig\"\n1437:         pre_dispatch:\n1438:           generate_summary: |\n1439:             STATE SUMMARY (auto-generated):\n1440:             Iteration: {current_iteration} of {max_iterations}\n1441:             Dimension: {next_dimension}\n1442:             Prior Findings: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1443:             Dimension Coverage: {dimensions_covered_list} ({dimension_coverage})\n1444:             Traceability: core={core_protocol_status} overlay={overlay_protocol_status}\n1445:             {resource_map_prompt_line}\n1446:             Coverage Age: {coverage_age}\n1447:             Last 2 ratios: {ratio_prev} -> {ratio_latest}\n1448:             Stuck count: {stuck_count}\n1449:             Provisional Verdict: {PASS|CONDITIONAL|FAIL|PENDING} hasAdvisories={has_advisories}\n1450:           render_prompt_pack:\n1451:             template_path: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl\"\n1452:             renderer: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/prompt-pack.ts#renderPromptPack\"\n1453:             output_path: \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md\"\n1454:             dry_run_output: \"Render in memory and print to terminal preview; do not write output_path.\"\n1455:             variables:\n1456:               state_summary: \"{state_summary}\"\n1457:               current_iteration: \"{current_iteration}\"\n1458:               max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n1459:               max_tool_calls_per_iteration: \"{config.maxToolCallsPerIteration}\"\n1460:               next_dimension: \"{next_dimension}\"\n1461:               review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n1462:               review_scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n1463:               p0_count: \"{p0_count}\"\n1464:               p1_count: \"{p1_count}\"\n1465:               p2_count: \"{p2_count}\"\n1466:               pivot_lineage: \"{pivot_lineage}\"\n1467:               saturated_directions: \"{saturated_directions}\"\n1468:               review_focus_block: \"{review_focus_block}\"\n1469:               unfinished_core_protocols_block: \"{unfinished_core_protocols_block}\"\n1470:               state_paths_config: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1471:               state_paths_state_log: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1472:               state_paths_findings_registry: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1473:               state_paths_strategy: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1474:               state_paths_iteration_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1475:               state_paths_delta_pattern: \"{state_paths.delta_pattern}\"\n1476:         pre_dispatch_audit:\n1477:           skip_when: \"config.executor.kind == 'native' or dry_run == true\"\n1478:           call: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts#writeFirstRecordExecutor\"\n1479:           args:\n1480:             stateLogPath: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1481:             executor: \"{config.executor}\"\n1482:             iteration: \"{current_iteration}\"\n1483:             sessionId: \"{session_id}\"\n1484:         branch_on: \"config.executor.kind\"\n1485:         cli_dispatch_args: '--loop-type review --repo-root \"{repo_root}\" --prompt-file \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --packet-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" --generation \"{generation}\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --model \"{config.executor.model}\" --reasoning-effort \"{config.executor.reasoningEffort}\" --service-tier \"{config.executor.serviceTier}\" --sandbox-mode \"{config.executor.sandboxMode}\" --timeout-seconds \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"'\n1486:         if_native:\n1487:           dispatch:\n1488:             agent: deep-review\n1489:             model: opus\n1490:             context_source: \"rendered_prompt_pack\"\n1491:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1492:           wait_for_completion: true\n1493:         if_cli_deepseek_harness:\n1494:           command: |\n1495:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-deepseek-harness {cli_dispatch_args} --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\"\n1496:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1497:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1498:           wait_for_completion: true\n1499:           notes:\n1500:             - \"cli-deepseek-harness single-executor: builds through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand), so the pinned harness release, the model allowlist and the route, lineage and guards patches stay one source of truth. runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1501:             - \"The harness starts in the artifact directory, never the repository root, with a fresh DSH_HOME outside the checkout. DSH_HOME, DSH_SPEC_FOLDER, SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED and AI_SESSION_CHILD reach the child through dispatchEnv, and the home is removed in a finally block. The event stream is judged and counted, not echoed\"\n1502:             - \"The prompt opens with a REPOSITORY ROOT line, because the prompt pack's paths and gateway call are repo-relative while the harness starts in the artifact directory\"\n1503:             - \"The child timeout is 30 s under the step timeout (at least half of it), so the finally block removes the home before any outer kill\"\n1504:             - \"validateDshCompletion judges a clean exit, so a plugin that did not activate or a missing final event records a crash dispatch_failure\"\n1505:             - \"Fails closed when the harness binary is absent, off its pinned release or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero). A requested cli-deepseek-harness executor never degrades to native\"\n1506:             - \"The command text never names the harness binary as a bare word, because the ancestry recursion guard reads the parent shell's command line\"\n1507:         if_cli_mistral_vibe:\n1508:           command: |\n1509:             node --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1510:             console.error('cli-mistral-vibe runs only as a fan-out lineage; rerun with --count=2 or a second --executor group, or choose another executor kind');\n1511:             process.exit(2);\n1512:             EOF\n1513:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1514:           wait_for_completion: true\n1515:           notes:\n1516:             - \"Fails closed before any dispatch receipt is written; the pre_dispatch_audit provenance row for the attempted executor remains\"\n1517:         if_cli_claude_code:\n1518:           command: |\n1519:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-claude-code {cli_dispatch_args} --claude-config-dir \"{optional_claude_config_dir}\"\n1520:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1521:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1522:           wait_for_completion: true\n1523:           render_hint:\n1524:             optional_claude_config_dir: |\n1525:               If config.executor.configDir is set and non-null, expand a leading ~ to HOME and bind that path.\n1526:               Otherwise expand to empty string.\n1527:           notes:\n1528:             - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so claude-code produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard + env allowlist enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n1529:             - \"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR is forwarded through guardContext.env (CLAUDE_ prefix is allowlisted) so account-specific Claude Code routing is preserved\"\n1530:             - \"permission-mode stays acceptEdits (review's existing iteration-write behavior); claude-code has no serviceTier flag\"\n1531:             - \"claude-code supports --effort for reasoning depth\"\n1532:         if_cli_opencode:\n1533:           command: |\n1534:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-opencode {cli_dispatch_args}\n1535:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1536:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1537:           wait_for_completion: true\n1538:           notes:\n1539:             - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so opencode produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard + env allowlist enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n1540:             - \"Fail closed before dispatch unless the rendered containment sections exist, --dir is an isolated linked worktree, the primary worktree is clean, and current-worktree changes are confined to artifact_dir both by name and after every path component is resolved through symlinks; append the recovery-baseline commit to state_log\"\n1541:             - \"buildLineageCommand returns empty input, so stdin is closed (EOF), equivalent to </dev/null\"\n1542:             - \"buildLineageCommand receives the route-proof preamble + iteration body as its message\"\n1543:             - \"buildLineageCommand maps reasoningEffort to the installed OpenCode version's supported option\"\n1544:             - \"buildLineageCommand resolves the OpenCode binary and version-correct argv for the configured sandboxMode\"\n1545:             - \"cli-opencode self-invocation guard: this single-executor branch must only run from a non-OpenCode dispatch surface (Claude Code/raw shell). Explicit parallel-detached cli-opencode fan-out is handled by step_fanout_spawn_cli/fanout-run.cjs, not this branch. the `cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode` mode's SKILL.md (`.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/SKILL.md`) §SELF-INVOCATION PROHIBITED contract is the authoritative gate\"\n1546:         if_cli_codex:\n1547:           command: |\n1548:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-codex {cli_dispatch_args}\n1549:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1550:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1551:           wait_for_completion: true\n1552:           notes:\n1553:             - \"PRE-DISPATCH RULE (read before running the script): when this run is ITSELF a fan-out CLI lineage — config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID / SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK / CODEX_SESSION_ID is present in the environment — the lineage IS the executor. Do NOT run this dispatch script. Perform the iteration in-process instead: read the rendered prompt at {state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md, do the review pass yourself, write the iteration file and the delta, and hand the iteration record to the append gateway (append-mode-event.cjs) exactly as the leaf contract requires, never writing the state log yourself, then continue to post_dispatch_validate.\"\n1554:             - \"Nested CLI dispatch from a lineage is a route violation, not a slow path: a codex lineage that runs this script spawns codex inside its own sandbox, where the child cannot initialize and every iteration fails. The script refuses that case before any spawn and before any dispatch receipt is written, exiting RECURSION_GUARD_EXIT_CODE; that refusal is a route error to fix, never a redispatchable executor failure.\"\n1555:             - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so codex produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard (CODEX_SESSION_ID) + env allowlist (CODEX_/OPENAI_/AZURE_OPENAI_) enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n1556:             - \"Fails closed when the codex binary is absent (exit 1) — parity with the fan-out cli-codex lineage guard in fanout-run.cjs; codex routing never degrades to native\"\n1557:             - \"codex exec reads the iteration prompt from stdin via the trailing '-' (input: promptBody); '-c model_reasoning_effort=' maps reasoning depth, default medium; '-c service_tier=' forwarded when configured\"\n1558:             - \"--sandbox workspace-write is required so the iteration can write its own iteration file/delta/state record (read-only would fail the post-dispatch artifact gate); -c approval_policy=never keeps it non-interactive; --model omitted when unset so ~/.codex/config.toml default applies\"\n1559:         if_cli_cursor:\n1560:           command: |\n1561:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-cursor {cli_dispatch_args}\n1562:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1563:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1564:           wait_for_completion: true\n1565:           notes:\n1566:             - \"cli-cursor single-executor: dispatches per-iteration through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand) so the enforced cli-cursor model allowlist + headless write flags stay one source of truth; runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1567:             - \"Fails closed when cursor-agent is absent or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero) — a requested cli-cursor executor never degrades to native\"\n1568:         if_cli_devin:\n1569:           command: |\n1570:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-devin {cli_dispatch_args}\n1571:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1572:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1573:           wait_for_completion: true\n1574:           notes:\n1575:             - \"cli-devin single-executor: dispatches per-iteration through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand) so the enforced cli-devin model allowlist + headless write flags stay one source of truth; runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1576:             - \"Fails closed when devin is absent or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero) — a requested cli-devin executor never degrades to native\"\n1577:         if_cli_pi:\n1578:           command: |\n1579:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-pi {cli_dispatch_args}\n1580:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1581:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1582:           wait_for_completion: true\n1583:           notes:\n1584:             - \"cli-pi single-executor: dispatches per-iteration through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand) so the enforced cli-pi model allowlist + headless write flags stay one source of truth; runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1585:             - \"Fails closed when pi is absent or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero) — a requested cli-pi executor never degrades to native\"\n1586:             - \"cli-deepseek-harness has its own single-executor branch, if_cli_deepseek_harness above, built through the same buildLineageCommand. Fan-out also runs the kind\"\n1587:         post_dispatch_validate:\n1588:           validator: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/post-dispatch-validate.ts#validateIterationOutputs\"\n1589:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/verify-iteration.cjs --loop-type review --artifact-dir {artifact_dir} --iteration {current_iteration}\"\n1590:           command_note: \"Mechanical leaf-reliability gate: exit 0 = complete; non-zero prints one machine reason (dispatch_failed|iteration_file_missing|iteration_verdict_missing|state_record_missing|route_proof_missing|route_proof_mismatch|delta_file_missing|executor_missing). dispatch_failed means the narrative is missing and the completion receipt shows a non-zero exit or a signal. executor_missing means the config names a non-native executor and neither the iteration record nor its iteration_start row names one. In a fan-out lineage it means the lineage's invocation-metadata.json does not name that executor. The script enforces the artifact + route-proof + executor contract instead of trusting the leaf to self-report, and a non-zero exit triggers on_failure.redispatch_once.\"\n1591:           assert_exists: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1592:           assert_appended: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1593:           assert_jsonl_fields: [type, iteration, mode, run, status, focus, dimensions, filesReviewed, findingsCount, findingsSummary, findingsNew, findingDetails, newFindingsRatio, sessionId, generation, lineageMode, timestamp, durationMs]\n1594:           route_proof:\n1595:             mode: review\n1596:             target_agent: deep-review\n1597:             agent_definition_loaded: true\n1598:             resolved_route: \"Resolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review\"\n1599:           dispatchReceipt:\n1600:             receiptDir: \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts\"\n1601:             dispatchId: \"review-i{current_iteration}-g{generation}\"\n1602:           sessionId: \"{session_id}\"\n1603:           assert_canonical_type: \"iteration\"\n1604:           assert_delta_file_exists: \"{state_paths.delta_pattern}\"\n1605:           assert_delta_file_has_iteration_record: true\n1606:           failure_reasons:\n1607:             - iteration_file_missing\n1608:             - iteration_file_empty\n1609:             - jsonl_not_appended\n1610:             - jsonl_missing_fields\n1611:             - jsonl_parse_error\n1612:             - jsonl_wrong_type\n1613:             - delta_file_missing\n1614:             - delta_file_empty\n1615:             - delta_file_missing_iteration_record\n1616:             - executor_missing\n1617:             - dispatch_failure_logged\n1618:             - v2_missing_ledger\n1619:             - v2_uncited_ledger_row\n1620:             - v2_broken_linked_finding\n1621:             - v2_shallow_finding_details\n1622:             - delta_iteration_id_mismatch\n1623:             - state_delta_iteration_mismatch\n1624:             - route_proof_missing\n1625:             - route_proof_mismatch\n1626:           warning_surface:\n1627:             source: \"result.warnings\"\n1628:             action: \"emit schema_advisory canonical conflict event\"\n1629:             severity: \"advisory\"\n1630:             event_shape: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"schema_advisory\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"iteration\":{current_iteration},\"warnings\":{result.warnings},\"severity\":\"advisory\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n1631:             note: \"Warnings do not fail dispatch. Hard failures still emit schema_mismatch through on_failure.\"\n1632:           on_failure:\n1633:             action: \"emit schema_mismatch canonical conflict event\"\n1634:             redispatch_once: \"On the FIRST failure of the mechanical command check for this iteration, re-run step_dispatch_iteration exactly once for the same iteration number, then re-run the check. If it still fails, record the iteration as error (per step_evaluate_results.on_missing_outputs) and continue. Never re-dispatch a given iteration more than once.\"\n1635:         record_executor_audit:\n1636:           skip_when: \"config.executor.kind == 'native'\"\n1637:           call: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts#appendExecutorAuditToLastRecord\"\n1638:           args:\n1639:             stateLogPath: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1640:             executor: \"{config.executor}\"\n1641:             sessionId: \"{session_id}\"\n1642: \n1643:       step_evaluate_results:\n1644:         action: \"Verify iteration outputs and extract metrics\"\n1645:         verify:\n1646:           - file_exists: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1647:           - jsonl_appended: \"New iteration record in state.jsonl\"\n1648:           - strategy_updated: \"Strategy.md has been modified\"\n1649:         extract:\n1650:           - newFindingsRatio: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1651:           - findings_count: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1652:           - severity_counts: \"From latest JSONL iteration record (P0, P1, P2)\"\n1653:           - dimensions: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1654:           - files_reviewed: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1655:           - status: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1656:           - reviewed_artifacts: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1657:           - traceability_checks: \"From latest JSONL iteration record when present\"\n1658:         on_missing_outputs:\n1659:           action: \"Inspect the latest dispatch record before handling missing outputs\"\n1660:           read:\n1661:             - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1662:           extract:\n1663:             - last_record: \"Parse the latest state.jsonl record after dispatch\"\n1664:           branch_on: \"last_record.type == 'event' AND last_record.event == 'dispatch_failure' AND last_record.executorUnavailable == true\"\n1665:           if_executor_unavailable:\n1666:             set: { reason: \"error\", stopReason: \"error\" }\n1667:             message: \"The {last_record.executor.kind} executor is unavailable ({last_record.matchedMarker}). Switch executor or wait, then resume this run.\"\n1668:             halt: true\n1669:             release_lock: step_release_lock\n1670:           if_other_failure:\n1671:             action: \"Mark iteration as 'error', continue to next\"\n1672:           # Canonical iteration record: include sessionId, generation, durationMs so the reducer can\n1673:           # persist the failure without dropping the iteration. Schema source: state-format.md §Iteration Records.\n1674:           # The row is staged for the append gateway: the state log is a projection of the\n1675:           # ledger, so a directly appended error row is dropped by the next refresh.\n1676:             command: |\n1677:               GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1678:               [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1679:               EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-iteration-error.XXXXXX\")\"\n1680:               cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1681:               {\"stem\":\"deep_review.iteration_error\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":{current_iteration},\"run\":{current_iteration},\"mode\":\"review\",\"status\":\"error\",\"focus\":\"{next_dimension}\",\"dimensions\":[\"{next_dimension}\"],\"filesReviewed\":[],\"findingsCount\":0,\"findingsSummary\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"findingsNew\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"findingDetails\":[],\"traceabilityChecks\":{\"summary\":{\"required\":0,\"executed\":0,\"pass\":0,\"partial\":0,\"fail\":0,\"blocked\":0,\"notApplicable\":0,\"gatingFailures\":0},\"results\":[]},\"newFindingsRatio\":0.0,\"durationMs\":0,\"sessionId\":\"{config.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.generation},\"lineageMode\":\"{config.lineageMode}\"}}\n1682:               DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1683:               node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1684:               RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1685:               rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1686:               exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1687: \n1688:       step_post_iteration_claim_adjudication:\n1689:         action: \"Validate typed claim-adjudication packets for any new P0/P1 findings and persist the result to state.jsonl so the next iteration's claimAdjudicationGate can read it\"\n1690:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1691:         verify:\n1692:           - typed_packets_present: \"Every new P0/P1 finding in review/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md contains a claim-adjudication JSON block\"\n1693:           - packet_fields: \"Each packet includes claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger\"\n1694:           - missing_packet_ids: \"List of new P0/P1 finding IDs that are missing a typed packet or field; empty array when all packets validate\"\n1695:         on_pass:\n1696:           set:\n1697:             claim_adjudication_passed: true\n1698:           # The row is staged as a canonical ledger event and appended by the gateway:\n1699:           # the state log is a projection of the ledger, so a write beside it is dropped\n1700:           # by the next refresh.\n1701:           command: |\n1702:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1703:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1704:             EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-claim-adjudication.XXXXXX\")\"\n1705:             cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1706:             {\"stem\":\"deep_review.claim_adjudication\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"passed\":true,\"activeP0P1\":{active_p0_p1_count},\"missingPackets\":[],\"reason\":null,\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}}\n1707:             DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1708:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1709:             RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1710:             rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1711:             exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1712:           log: \"Claim adjudication passed for iteration {current_iteration}. All new P0/P1 findings have typed packets.\"\n1713:         on_fail:\n1714:           action: \"Mark the iteration as invalid for convergence. The next iteration's claimAdjudicationGate (step_check_convergence step 0) reads the persisted `passed: false` event and vetoes STOP until a follow-up iteration rewrites the packets.\"\n1715:           set:\n1716:             claim_adjudication_passed: false\n1717:           command: |\n1718:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1719:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1720:             EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-claim-adjudication.XXXXXX\")\"\n1721:             cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1722:             {\"stem\":\"deep_review.claim_adjudication\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"passed\":false,\"activeP0P1\":{active_p0_p1_count},\"missingPackets\":{missing_packet_ids},\"reason\":\"Missing typed packet fields for new P0/P1 findings\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}}\n1723:             DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1724:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1725:             RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1726:             rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1727:             exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1728:           log: \"Claim adjudication incomplete for new P0/P1 findings. Event persisted. The next iteration's step_check_convergence claim-adjudication pre-check will veto STOP while `passed: false` remains the latest event and active P0/P1 > 0.\"\n1729: \n1730:       step_reduce_review_state:\n1731:         action: \"Run reducer to refresh the canonical findings registry before dashboard generation\"\n1732:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1733:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\"\n1734:         read:\n1735:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1736:           - \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1737:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1738:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1739:         write:\n1740:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1741:           - \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n1742:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1743:         failure_modes:\n1744:           malformed_delta: \"skip + warn\"\n1745:           missing_iteration_file: \"no-op + error\"\n1746:           schema_mismatch: \"reject + conflict event\"\n1747:         guarantee: \"Idempotent for identical inputs\"\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1748]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 1418-1747\n1418:       step_dispatch_iteration:\n1419:         action: \"Dispatch @deep-review agent for one review iteration\"\n1420:         dry_run_boundary: \"dispatch\"\n1421:         dry_run_preview:\n1422:           before_halt:\n1423:             - \"Generate the state summary.\"\n1424:             - \"Render the prompt pack to terminal preview without writing the prompt file.\"\n1425:             - \"Show the selected executor branch and command or native dispatch target that would run.\"\n1426:         pre_dispatch_refresh_lock:\n1427:           action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately before the dispatch starts\"\n1428:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n1429:           on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. Run step_release_lock and stop rather than dispatch without it.\"\n1430:         post_dispatch_refresh_lock:\n1431:           action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately after the dispatch returns\"\n1432:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n1433:           on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. Run step_release_lock and stop rather than continue without it.\"\n1434:         resolve_executor:\n1435:           source: \"config.executor\"\n1436:           loader: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts#parseExecutorConfig\"\n1437:         pre_dispatch:\n1438:           generate_summary: |\n1439:             STATE SUMMARY (auto-generated):\n1440:             Iteration: {current_iteration} of {max_iterations}\n1441:             Dimension: {next_dimension}\n1442:             Prior Findings: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1443:             Dimension Coverage: {dimensions_covered_list} ({dimension_coverage})\n1444:             Traceability: core={core_protocol_status} overlay={overlay_protocol_status}\n1445:             {resource_map_prompt_line}\n1446:             Coverage Age: {coverage_age}\n1447:             Last 2 ratios: {ratio_prev} -> {ratio_latest}\n1448:             Stuck count: {stuck_count}\n1449:             Provisional Verdict: {PASS|CONDITIONAL|FAIL|PENDING} hasAdvisories={has_advisories}\n1450:           render_prompt_pack:\n1451:             template_path: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl\"\n1452:             renderer: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/prompt-pack.ts#renderPromptPack\"\n1453:             output_path: \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md\"\n1454:             dry_run_output: \"Render in memory and print to terminal preview; do not write output_path.\"\n1455:             variables:\n1456:               state_summary: \"{state_summary}\"\n1457:               current_iteration: \"{current_iteration}\"\n1458:               max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n1459:               max_tool_calls_per_iteration: \"{config.maxToolCallsPerIteration}\"\n1460:               next_dimension: \"{next_dimension}\"\n1461:               review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n1462:               review_scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n1463:               p0_count: \"{p0_count}\"\n1464:               p1_count: \"{p1_count}\"\n1465:               p2_count: \"{p2_count}\"\n1466:               pivot_lineage: \"{pivot_lineage}\"\n1467:               saturated_directions: \"{saturated_directions}\"\n1468:               review_focus_block: \"{review_focus_block}\"\n1469:               unfinished_core_protocols_block: \"{unfinished_core_protocols_block}\"\n1470:               state_paths_config: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1471:               state_paths_state_log: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1472:               state_paths_findings_registry: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1473:               state_paths_strategy: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1474:               state_paths_iteration_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1475:               state_paths_delta_pattern: \"{state_paths.delta_pattern}\"\n1476:         pre_dispatch_audit:\n1477:           skip_when: \"config.executor.kind == 'native' or dry_run == true\"\n1478:           call: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts#writeFirstRecordExecutor\"\n1479:           args:\n1480:             stateLogPath: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1481:             executor: \"{config.executor}\"\n1482:             iteration: \"{current_iteration}\"\n1483:             sessionId: \"{session_id}\"\n1484:         branch_on: \"config.executor.kind\"\n1485:         cli_dispatch_args: '--loop-type review --repo-root \"{repo_root}\" --prompt-file \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --packet-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" --generation \"{generation}\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --model \"{config.executor.model}\" --reasoning-effort \"{config.executor.reasoningEffort}\" --service-tier \"{config.executor.serviceTier}\" --sandbox-mode \"{config.executor.sandboxMode}\" --timeout-seconds \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"'\n1486:         if_native:\n1487:           dispatch:\n1488:             agent: deep-review\n1489:             model: opus\n1490:             context_source: \"rendered_prompt_pack\"\n1491:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1492:           wait_for_completion: true\n1493:         if_cli_deepseek_harness:\n1494:           command: |\n1495:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-deepseek-harness {cli_dispatch_args} --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\"\n1496:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1497:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1498:           wait_for_completion: true\n1499:           notes:\n1500:             - \"cli-deepseek-harness single-executor: builds through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand), so the pinned harness release, the model allowlist and the route, lineage and guards patches stay one source of truth. runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1501:             - \"The harness starts in the artifact directory, never the repository root, with a fresh DSH_HOME outside the checkout. DSH_HOME, DSH_SPEC_FOLDER, SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED and AI_SESSION_CHILD reach the child through dispatchEnv, and the home is removed in a finally block. The event stream is judged and counted, not echoed\"\n1502:             - \"The prompt opens with a REPOSITORY ROOT line, because the prompt pack's paths and gateway call are repo-relative while the harness starts in the artifact directory\"\n1503:             - \"The child timeout is 30 s under the step timeout (at least half of it), so the finally block removes the home before any outer kill\"\n1504:             - \"validateDshCompletion judges a clean exit, so a plugin that did not activate or a missing final event records a crash dispatch_failure\"\n1505:             - \"Fails closed when the harness binary is absent, off its pinned release or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero). A requested cli-deepseek-harness executor never degrades to native\"\n1506:             - \"The command text never names the harness binary as a bare word, because the ancestry recursion guard reads the parent shell's command line\"\n1507:         if_cli_mistral_vibe:\n1508:           command: |\n1509:             node --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1510:             console.error('cli-mistral-vibe runs only as a fan-out lineage; rerun with --count=2 or a second --executor group, or choose another executor kind');\n1511:             process.exit(2);\n1512:             EOF\n1513:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1514:           wait_for_completion: true\n1515:           notes:\n1516:             - \"Fails closed before any dispatch receipt is written; the pre_dispatch_audit provenance row for the attempted executor remains\"\n1517:         if_cli_claude_code:\n1518:           command: |\n1519:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-claude-code {cli_dispatch_args} --claude-config-dir \"{optional_claude_config_dir}\"\n1520:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1521:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1522:           wait_for_completion: true\n1523:           render_hint:\n1524:             optional_claude_config_dir: |\n1525:               If config.executor.configDir is set and non-null, expand a leading ~ to HOME and bind that path.\n1526:               Otherwise expand to empty string.\n1527:           notes:\n1528:             - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so claude-code produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard + env allowlist enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n1529:             - \"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR is forwarded through guardContext.env (CLAUDE_ prefix is allowlisted) so account-specific Claude Code routing is preserved\"\n1530:             - \"permission-mode stays acceptEdits (review's existing iteration-write behavior); claude-code has no serviceTier flag\"\n1531:             - \"claude-code supports --effort for reasoning depth\"\n1532:         if_cli_opencode:\n1533:           command: |\n1534:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-opencode {cli_dispatch_args}\n1535:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1536:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1537:           wait_for_completion: true\n1538:           notes:\n1539:             - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so opencode produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard + env allowlist enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n1540:             - \"Fail closed before dispatch unless the rendered containment sections exist, --dir is an isolated linked worktree, the primary worktree is clean, and current-worktree changes are confined to artifact_dir both by name and after every path component is resolved through symlinks; append the recovery-baseline commit to state_log\"\n1541:             - \"buildLineageCommand returns empty input, so stdin is closed (EOF), equivalent to </dev/null\"\n1542:             - \"buildLineageCommand receives the route-proof preamble + iteration body as its message\"\n1543:             - \"buildLineageCommand maps reasoningEffort to the installed OpenCode version's supported option\"\n1544:             - \"buildLineageCommand resolves the OpenCode binary and version-correct argv for the configured sandboxMode\"\n1545:             - \"cli-opencode self-invocation guard: this single-executor branch must only run from a non-OpenCode dispatch surface (Claude Code/raw shell). Explicit parallel-detached cli-opencode fan-out is handled by step_fanout_spawn_cli/fanout-run.cjs, not this branch. the `cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode` mode's SKILL.md (`.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/SKILL.md`) §SELF-INVOCATION PROHIBITED contract is the authoritative gate\"\n1546:         if_cli_codex:\n1547:           command: |\n1548:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-codex {cli_dispatch_args}\n1549:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1550:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1551:           wait_for_completion: true\n1552:           notes:\n1553:             - \"PRE-DISPATCH RULE (read before running the script): when this run is ITSELF a fan-out CLI lineage — config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID / SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK / CODEX_SESSION_ID is present in the environment — the lineage IS the executor. Do NOT run this dispatch script. Perform the iteration in-process instead: read the rendered prompt at {state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md, do the review pass yourself, write the iteration file and the delta, and hand the iteration record to the append gateway (append-mode-event.cjs) exactly as the leaf contract requires, never writing the state log yourself, then continue to post_dispatch_validate.\"\n1554:             - \"Nested CLI dispatch from a lineage is a route violation, not a slow path: a codex lineage that runs this script spawns codex inside its own sandbox, where the child cannot initialize and every iteration fails. The script refuses that case before any spawn and before any dispatch receipt is written, exiting RECURSION_GUARD_EXIT_CODE; that refusal is a route error to fix, never a redispatchable executor failure.\"\n1555:             - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so codex produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard (CODEX_SESSION_ID) + env allowlist (CODEX_/OPENAI_/AZURE_OPENAI_) enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n1556:             - \"Fails closed when the codex binary is absent (exit 1) — parity with the fan-out cli-codex lineage guard in fanout-run.cjs; codex routing never degrades to native\"\n1557:             - \"codex exec reads the iteration prompt from stdin via the trailing '-' (input: promptBody); '-c model_reasoning_effort=' maps reasoning depth, default medium; '-c service_tier=' forwarded when configured\"\n1558:             - \"--sandbox workspace-write is required so the iteration can write its own iteration file/delta/state record (read-only would fail the post-dispatch artifact gate); -c approval_policy=never keeps it non-interactive; --model omitted when unset so ~/.codex/config.toml default applies\"\n1559:         if_cli_cursor:\n1560:           command: |\n1561:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-cursor {cli_dispatch_args}\n1562:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1563:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1564:           wait_for_completion: true\n1565:           notes:\n1566:             - \"cli-cursor single-executor: dispatches per-iteration through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand) so the enforced cli-cursor model allowlist + headless write flags stay one source of truth; runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1567:             - \"Fails closed when cursor-agent is absent or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero) — a requested cli-cursor executor never degrades to native\"\n1568:         if_cli_devin:\n1569:           command: |\n1570:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-devin {cli_dispatch_args}\n1571:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1572:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1573:           wait_for_completion: true\n1574:           notes:\n1575:             - \"cli-devin single-executor: dispatches per-iteration through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand) so the enforced cli-devin model allowlist + headless write flags stay one source of truth; runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1576:             - \"Fails closed when devin is absent or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero) — a requested cli-devin executor never degrades to native\"\n1577:         if_cli_pi:\n1578:           command: |\n1579:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-pi {cli_dispatch_args}\n1580:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1581:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1582:           wait_for_completion: true\n1583:           notes:\n1584:             - \"cli-pi single-executor: dispatches per-iteration through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand) so the enforced cli-pi model allowlist + headless write flags stay one source of truth; runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1585:             - \"Fails closed when pi is absent or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero) — a requested cli-pi executor never degrades to native\"\n1586:             - \"cli-deepseek-harness has its own single-executor branch, if_cli_deepseek_harness above, built through the same buildLineageCommand. Fan-out also runs the kind\"\n1587:         post_dispatch_validate:\n1588:           validator: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/post-dispatch-validate.ts#validateIterationOutputs\"\n1589:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/verify-iteration.cjs --loop-type review --artifact-dir {artifact_dir} --iteration {current_iteration}\"\n1590:           command_note: \"Mechanical leaf-reliability gate: exit 0 = complete; non-zero prints one machine reason (dispatch_failed|iteration_file_missing|iteration_verdict_missing|state_record_missing|route_proof_missing|route_proof_mismatch|delta_file_missing|executor_missing). dispatch_failed means the narrative is missing and the completion receipt shows a non-zero exit or a signal. executor_missing means the config names a non-native executor and neither the iteration record nor its iteration_start row names one. In a fan-out lineage it means the lineage's invocation-metadata.json does not name that executor. The script enforces the artifact + route-proof + executor contract instead of trusting the leaf to self-report, and a non-zero exit triggers on_failure.redispatch_once.\"\n1591:           assert_exists: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1592:           assert_appended: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1593:           assert_jsonl_fields: [type, iteration, mode, run, status, focus, dimensions, filesReviewed, findingsCount, findingsSummary, findingsNew, findingDetails, newFindingsRatio, sessionId, generation, lineageMode, timestamp, durationMs]\n1594:           route_proof:\n1595:             mode: review\n1596:             target_agent: deep-review\n1597:             agent_definition_loaded: true\n1598:             resolved_route: \"Resolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review\"\n1599:           dispatchReceipt:\n1600:             receiptDir: \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts\"\n1601:             dispatchId: \"review-i{current_iteration}-g{generation}\"\n1602:           sessionId: \"{session_id}\"\n1603:           assert_canonical_type: \"iteration\"\n1604:           assert_delta_file_exists: \"{state_paths.delta_pattern}\"\n1605:           assert_delta_file_has_iteration_record: true\n1606:           failure_reasons:\n1607:             - iteration_file_missing\n1608:             - iteration_file_empty\n1609:             - jsonl_not_appended\n1610:             - jsonl_missing_fields\n1611:             - jsonl_parse_error\n1612:             - jsonl_wrong_type\n1613:             - delta_file_missing\n1614:             - delta_file_empty\n1615:             - delta_file_missing_iteration_record\n1616:             - executor_missing\n1617:             - dispatch_failure_logged\n1618:             - v2_missing_ledger\n1619:             - v2_uncited_ledger_row\n1620:             - v2_broken_linked_finding\n1621:             - v2_shallow_finding_details\n1622:             - delta_iteration_id_mismatch\n1623:             - state_delta_iteration_mismatch\n1624:             - route_proof_missing\n1625:             - route_proof_mismatch\n1626:           warning_surface:\n1627:             source: \"result.warnings\"\n1628:             action: \"emit schema_advisory canonical conflict event\"\n1629:             severity: \"advisory\"\n1630:             event_shape: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"schema_advisory\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"iteration\":{current_iteration},\"warnings\":{result.warnings},\"severity\":\"advisory\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n1631:             note: \"Warnings do not fail dispatch. Hard failures still emit schema_mismatch through on_failure.\"\n1632:           on_failure:\n1633:             action: \"emit schema_mismatch canonical conflict event\"\n1634:             redispatch_once: \"On the FIRST failure of the mechanical command check for this iteration, re-run step_dispatch_iteration exactly once for the same iteration number, then re-run the check. If it still fails, record the iteration as error (per step_evaluate_results.on_missing_outputs) and continue. Never re-dispatch a given iteration more than once.\"\n1635:         record_executor_audit:\n1636:           skip_when: \"config.executor.kind == 'native'\"\n1637:           call: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts#appendExecutorAuditToLastRecord\"\n1638:           args:\n1639:             stateLogPath: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1640:             executor: \"{config.executor}\"\n1641:             sessionId: \"{session_id}\"\n1642: \n1643:       step_evaluate_results:\n1644:         action: \"Verify iteration outputs and extract metrics\"\n1645:         verify:\n1646:           - file_exists: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1647:           - jsonl_appended: \"New iteration record in state.jsonl\"\n1648:           - strategy_updated: \"Strategy.md has been modified\"\n1649:         extract:\n1650:           - newFindingsRatio: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1651:           - findings_count: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1652:           - severity_counts: \"From latest JSONL iteration record (P0, P1, P2)\"\n1653:           - dimensions: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1654:           - files_reviewed: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1655:           - status: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1656:           - reviewed_artifacts: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1657:           - traceability_checks: \"From latest JSONL iteration record when present\"\n1658:         on_missing_outputs:\n1659:           action: \"Inspect the latest dispatch record before handling missing outputs\"\n1660:           read:\n1661:             - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1662:           extract:\n1663:             - last_record: \"Parse the latest state.jsonl record after dispatch\"\n1664:           branch_on: \"last_record.type == 'event' AND last_record.event == 'dispatch_failure' AND last_record.executorUnavailable == true\"\n1665:           if_executor_unavailable:\n1666:             set: { reason: \"error\", stopReason: \"error\" }\n1667:             message: \"The {last_record.executor.kind} executor is unavailable ({last_record.matchedMarker}). Switch executor or wait, then resume this run.\"\n1668:             halt: true\n1669:             release_lock: step_release_lock\n1670:           if_other_failure:\n1671:             action: \"Mark iteration as 'error', continue to next\"\n1672:           # Canonical iteration record: include sessionId, generation, durationMs so the reducer can\n1673:           # persist the failure without dropping the iteration. Schema source: state-format.md §Iteration Records.\n1674:           # The row is staged for the append gateway: the state log is a projection of the\n1675:           # ledger, so a directly appended error row is dropped by the next refresh.\n1676:             command: |\n1677:               GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1678:               [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1679:               EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-iteration-error.XXXXXX\")\"\n1680:               cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1681:               {\"stem\":\"deep_review.iteration_error\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":{current_iteration},\"run\":{current_iteration},\"mode\":\"review\",\"status\":\"error\",\"focus\":\"{next_dimension}\",\"dimensions\":[\"{next_dimension}\"],\"filesReviewed\":[],\"findingsCount\":0,\"findingsSummary\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"findingsNew\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"findingDetails\":[],\"traceabilityChecks\":{\"summary\":{\"required\":0,\"executed\":0,\"pass\":0,\"partial\":0,\"fail\":0,\"blocked\":0,\"notApplicable\":0,\"gatingFailures\":0},\"results\":[]},\"newFindingsRatio\":0.0,\"durationMs\":0,\"sessionId\":\"{config.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.generation},\"lineageMode\":\"{config.lineageMode}\"}}\n1682:               DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1683:               node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1684:               RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1685:               rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1686:               exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1687: \n1688:       step_post_iteration_claim_adjudication:\n1689:         action: \"Validate typed claim-adjudication packets for any new P0/P1 findings and persist the result to state.jsonl so the next iteration's claimAdjudicationGate can read it\"\n1690:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1691:         verify:\n1692:           - typed_packets_present: \"Every new P0/P1 finding in review/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md contains a claim-adjudication JSON block\"\n1693:           - packet_fields: \"Each packet includes claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger\"\n1694:           - missing_packet_ids: \"List of new P0/P1 finding IDs that are missing a typed packet or field; empty array when all packets validate\"\n1695:         on_pass:\n1696:           set:\n1697:             claim_adjudication_passed: true\n1698:           # The row is staged as a canonical ledger event and appended by the gateway:\n1699:           # the state log is a projection of the ledger, so a write beside it is dropped\n1700:           # by the next refresh.\n1701:           command: |\n1702:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1703:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1704:             EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-claim-adjudication.XXXXXX\")\"\n1705:             cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1706:             {\"stem\":\"deep_review.claim_adjudication\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"passed\":true,\"activeP0P1\":{active_p0_p1_count},\"missingPackets\":[],\"reason\":null,\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}}\n1707:             DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1708:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1709:             RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1710:             rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1711:             exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1712:           log: \"Claim adjudication passed for iteration {current_iteration}. All new P0/P1 findings have typed packets.\"\n1713:         on_fail:\n1714:           action: \"Mark the iteration as invalid for convergence. The next iteration's claimAdjudicationGate (step_check_convergence step 0) reads the persisted `passed: false` event and vetoes STOP until a follow-up iteration rewrites the packets.\"\n1715:           set:\n1716:             claim_adjudication_passed: false\n1717:           command: |\n1718:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1719:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1720:             EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-claim-adjudication.XXXXXX\")\"\n1721:             cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1722:             {\"stem\":\"deep_review.claim_adjudication\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"passed\":false,\"activeP0P1\":{active_p0_p1_count},\"missingPackets\":{missing_packet_ids},\"reason\":\"Missing typed packet fields for new P0/P1 findings\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}}\n1723:             DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1724:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1725:             RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1726:             rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1727:             exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1728:           log: \"Claim adjudication incomplete for new P0/P1 findings. Event persisted. The next iteration's step_check_convergence claim-adjudication pre-check will veto STOP while `passed: false` remains the latest event and active P0/P1 > 0.\"\n1729: \n1730:       step_reduce_review_state:\n1731:         action: \"Run reducer to refresh the canonical findings registry before dashboard generation\"\n1732:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1733:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\"\n1734:         read:\n1735:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1736:           - \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1737:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1738:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1739:         write:\n1740:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1741:           - \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n1742:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1743:         failure_modes:\n1744:           malformed_delta: \"skip + warn\"\n1745:           missing_iteration_file: \"no-op + error\"\n1746:           schema_mismatch: \"reject + conflict event\"\n1747:         guarantee: \"Idempotent for identical inputs\"\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1748]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":330,\"offset\":1418,\"path\":\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830078472,"end":1794830078484}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794830079799,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","part":{"id":"prt_1e4359737001clIsJv637K3A5S","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","messageID":"msg_1e43588a8001rkRrKbqh4T2vyO","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"05528263d614a2c6dc32246ba283c6496cb5833a","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":745,"output":82,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":65408,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794830082673,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","part":{"id":"prt_1e435a271001TnV26YPBRt0tHe","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","messageID":"msg_1e435973e001hzhjsCOJZXNYQJ","type":"step-start","snapshot":"05528263d614a2c6dc32246ba283c6496cb5833a"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830083423,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","part":{"partID":"prt_1e435a3ad0021Mx2JeMNlXzdBo","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","messageID":"msg_1e435973e001hzhjsCOJZXNYQJ","type":"tool","id":"call_a0eb248ee36846f5ba7042ed","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":330,"offset":1748,"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 1748-2077\n1748:         note: \"Reducer outputs findingsRegistry, dashboardMetrics, and strategyUpdates. Re-running the same inputs must be idempotent.\"\n1749: \n1750:       step_graph_upsert:\n1751:         action: \"Project canonical review coverage plus optional graphEvents into graph nodes and edges, then upsert it\"\n1752:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1753:         read:\n1754:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1755:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1756:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1757:         transform: |\n1758:           1. Read the latest iteration JSONL record after reducer completion.\n1759:           2. Seed one stable DIMENSION node for every configured review dimension, falling back to correctness, security, traceability, and maintainability.\n1760:           3. Seed one stable FILE node for every latest-record filesReviewed entry and emit a COVERS edge from each latest-record dimension to each reviewed file.\n1761:           4. Merge optional graphEvents nodes after normalizing type = uppercase(event.kind || event.nodeKind || event.type); keep only DIMENSION, FILE, FINDING, EVIDENCE, REMEDIATION, BUG_CLASS, INVARIANT, PRODUCER, CONSUMER, TEST.\n1762:           5. Merge optional graphEvents edges after normalizing relation = uppercase(event.relation); keep only COVERS, EVIDENCE_FOR, CONTRADICTS, RESOLVES, CONFIRMS, ESCALATES, IN_DIMENSION, IN_FILE.\n1763:           6. Emit nodes as { id, type, name, iteration, metadata } and edges as { id, relation, sourceId, targetId, metadata }, deduplicated by id.\n1764:           7. Discard malformed or unknown optional events without discarding canonical dimension and file coverage.\n1765:         bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{session_id}\\\" --nodes '{graph_nodes_json}' --edges '{graph_edges_json}'\"\n1766:         note: \"Invoke the runtime script directly. Canonical iteration fields provide baseline coverage; graphEvents add richer evidence.\"\n1767:         outputs:\n1768:           - graph_nodes_json: \"JSON array of canonical and optional review graph nodes\"\n1769:           - graph_edges_json: \"JSON array of canonical and optional review graph edges\"\n1770: \n1771:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Iteration ───\n1772:       gate_post_iteration:\n1773:         applies_to: confirm\n1774:         type: approval_gate\n1775:         purpose: \"Show iteration findings and get approval for next step\"\n1776:         present: |\n1777:           ## Review Iteration {current_iteration} Results\n1778: \n1779:           **Dimensions**: {dimensions}\n1780:           **New Findings**: {findings_count} (P0={severity_counts.P0} P1={severity_counts.P1} P2={severity_counts.P2})\n1781:           **newFindingsRatio**: {newFindingsRatio}\n1782:           **Status**: {status}\n1783:           **Cumulative Findings**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1784:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n1785:           **Traceability**: {traceability_checks.summary}\n1786:           **Stuck Count**: {stuck_count}\n1787: \n1788:           **Recent Iteration Summary**:\n1789:           {last_3_summaries}\n1790: \n1791:           Options:\n1792:           A) Continue to next iteration\n1793:           B) Continue with adjusted focus: [user provides]\n1794:           C) Stop loop and synthesize\n1795:           D) Cancel entirely\n1796:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1797:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1798:         on_A: { proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n1799:         on_B: { action: \"Set next_dimension to user's choice in strategy.md\", proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n1800:         on_C: { set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }, run_first: record_terminal_gates, proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n1801:         on_D: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n1802: \n1803:       step_update_tracking:\n1804:         action: \"Update loop tracking variables\"\n1805:         set:\n1806:           current_iteration: \"{current_iteration + 1}\"\n1807:         log: \"Iteration {N} complete. Dimensions: {dimensions}. newFindingsRatio: {newFindingsRatio}. Findings: P0={severity_counts.P0} P1={severity_counts.P1} P2={severity_counts.P2}.\"\n1808: \n1809:       step_loop_decision:\n1810:         action: \"Return to step_read_state for next iteration\"\n1811:         goto: step_read_state\n1812: \n1813:   # ════════\n1814:   # PHASE 3: SYNTHESIS\n1815:   # ════════\n1816:   phase_synthesis:\n1817:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n1818:     steps:\n1819: \n1820:       step_fanout_merge:\n1821:         description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n1822:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1823:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n1824:         command: |\n1825:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n1826:             --loop-type review \\\n1827:             --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n1828:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1829:         wait_for_completion: true\n1830:         bind_from_output:\n1831:           p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n1832:           p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n1833:           p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n1834:           failed_required_gate_ids: \"failed_required_gate_ids\"\n1835:           search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n1836: \n1837:       step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n1838:         action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n1839:         read:\n1840:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1841:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1842:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1843:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1844:         read_patterns:\n1845:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n1846:         extract:\n1847:           - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n1848:           - highest_run: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in those logs in stable lineage order, else 0; otherwise take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in the root state log, else 0. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n1849:           - current_iteration: \"max(highest_run, iteration_count) + 1\"\n1850:           - p0_count: \"When step_fanout_merge bound it, keep the merged value; the fan-out verdict reads it. Otherwise the count of open findings in {state_paths.findings_registry} with status active and severity P0, for the pre-synthesis display only.\"\n1851:           - p1_count: \"Same rule as p0_count, for severity P1.\"\n1852:           - p2_count: \"Same rule as p0_count, for severity P2.\"\n1853:           - failed_required_gate_ids: \"When step_fanout_merge bound it, keep the merged value. Otherwise take failedRequiredGateIds from the last line of {state_paths.state_log} with type === 'event' and event === 'terminal_gates', else []. Read the state log, not the registry: the reducer last ran before the stop wrote that row.\"\n1854:           - dimensions_covered: \"List of reviewed dimensions\"\n1855:           - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total\"\n1856:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"For spec-folder targets only: if level is 2+ and acceptance-criteria.md exists and implementation-summary.md is in-progress or later, surface the AC_COVERAGE advisory status; otherwise mark exempt.\"\n1857:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records\"\n1858:           - reason: \"Use the latest stop reason if present: read stopReason from the last line of {state_paths.state_log} with type === 'event' and event === 'terminal_gates' when it is newer than the latest stop event, since a manual stop is stored only there; else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused, maxDurationReached.)\"\n1859: \n1860:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Pre-Synthesis ───\n1861:       gate_pre_synthesis:\n1862:         applies_to: confirm\n1863:         type: approval_gate\n1864:         purpose: \"Show all accumulated findings and get approval to synthesize\"\n1865:         present: |\n1866:           ## Review Loop Complete\n1867: \n1868:           **Total Iterations**: {iteration_count}\n1869:           **Stop Reason**: {reason}\n1870:           **Cumulative Findings**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1871:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n1872:           **Recent Iteration Summary**: {last_3_summaries}\n1873: \n1874:           Review the iteration files in `{state_paths.iteration_dir}/` if you want more detail before synthesis.\n1875: \n1876:           Options:\n1877:           A) Proceed to synthesis (compile review/review-report.md)\n1878:           B) Run more iterations (increase max or focus on specific dimension)\n1879:           C) Cancel (keep iteration files)\n1880:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1881:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1882:         on_A: { proceed_to: step_read_all_iterations }\n1883:         on_B: { action: \"Increase max_iterations or adjust focus, return to loop. When reason is maxDurationReached, raise maxDurationMinutes in the config too, or the duration check stops the loop again and writes another terminal record\", proceed_to: phase_loop }\n1884:         on_C: { action: \"Cancel synthesis, keep artifacts\", status: \"PARTIAL\" }\n1885: \n1886:       step_read_all_iterations:\n1887:         action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n1888:         read_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n1889:         read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1890: \n1891:       step_build_finding_registry:\n1892:         action: \"Build deduplicated finding registry from all iterations\"\n1893:         algorithm: |\n1894:           1. Extract all findings from iteration JSONL delta files\n1895:           2. Compute content_hash for each finding (emission requirement):\n1896:              content_hash = sha256(file_path + \"\\u001f\" + line_range + \"\\u001f\" + finding_type + \"\\u001f\" + normalized_description_80chars)\n1897:              Normalized description = whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, first 80 chars of the finding description.\n1898:           3. Two-tier dedup:\n1899:              PRIMARY: group by content_hash field\n1900:                - Same content_hash, multiple dimensions → single finding, merged `dimensions: [<all>]` array\n1901:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n1902:              FALLBACK (legacy records lacking content_hash): file:line + normalized_title\n1903:                - Same file:line, multiple dimensions → single finding, multiple dimension tags\n1904:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n1905:           4. Track finding lifecycle:\n1906:              - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n1907:              - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n1908:              - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n1909:           5. Resolve contradictions:\n1910:              - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n1911:              - Determine final severity and status\n1912:           6. Count only 'active' findings for totals. These totals are narrative only: step_derive_verdict reads the registry file after the self-check refreshes it, and the report and the closeout state its counts as the counts the verdict used.\n1913:         outputs:\n1914:           - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n1915: \n1916:       # Adjudication persistence: the Referee's call becomes a claim_adjudication row per\n1917:       # finding, so the registry the verdict reads carries the final severity. A false\n1918:       # positive is recorded as `none`, the scale value for a claim that is not a finding.\n1919:       step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n1920:         action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n1921:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1922:         algorithm: |\n1923:           For each active P0/P1 finding:\n1924:             1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n1925:             2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n1926:             3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n1927:           Record one `<findingId> <finalSeverity>` pair for every call the Referee made\n1928:           here: the severity it settled on, or `none` when it called the finding a false\n1929:           positive. An empty list means the Referee changed nothing.\n1930:           On a single-executor run, append one deep_review.claim_adjudication row per pair\n1931:           through the gateway, then refresh the registry once. The verdict step that\n1932:           follows reads the refreshed registry, so a downgrade or a false positive changes\n1933:           the counts the verdict, the report and the closeout all use.\n1934:           On a fan-out root, record the pairs for the report only: the root has no state\n1935:           log before closeout, and the merged lineage counts are what that verdict reads.\n1936:         extract:\n1937:           - selfcheck_adjudications: \"One `<findingId> <finalSeverity>` pair per line, using the findingId exactly as it appears in openFindings of {state_paths.findings_registry}, empty when the Referee changed nothing\"\n1938:           - adjudication_mode: \"`mode` of the latest claim_adjudication gate row (the newest one without a findingId), else \\\"review\\\"\"\n1939:           - adjudication_run: \"`run` of that gate row, else {highest_run}\"\n1940:           - adjudication_passed: \"`passed` of that gate row, else true\"\n1941:           - adjudication_active_p0_p1: \"`activeP0P1` of that gate row, else {p0_count} plus {p1_count}\"\n1942:           - adjudication_missing_packets: \"`missingPackets` of that gate row as a JSON array, else []\"\n1943:           - adjudication_reason: \"`reason` of that gate row as a JSON value, else \\\"adversarial self-check\\\"\"\n1944:         branch_on: \"config.fanout\"\n1945:         if_present:\n1946:           action: \"Record the pairs in the Executive Summary for reference. Do not append: a fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, and each lineage already adjudicated its own findings, so the merged counts are the authority here.\"\n1947:         if_absent:\n1948:           # The row is staged for the append gateway: the state log is a projection of the\n1949:           # ledger, so a row written beside it is dropped by the next refresh.\n1950:           command: |\n1951:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1952:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1953:             RUN_DIR=\"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\"\n1954:             while read -r FINDING_ID FINAL_SEVERITY; do\n1955:             [ -n \"$FINDING_ID\" ] || continue\n1956:             EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-claim-adjudication.XXXXXX\")\"\n1957:             cat <<DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1958:             {\"stem\":\"deep_review.claim_adjudication\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"{adjudication_mode}\",\"run\":{adjudication_run},\"passed\":{adjudication_passed},\"activeP0P1\":{adjudication_active_p0_p1},\"missingPackets\":{adjudication_missing_packets},\"reason\":{adjudication_reason},\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"findingId\":\"$FINDING_ID\",\"finalSeverity\":\"$FINAL_SEVERITY\"}}\n1959:             DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1960:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$RUN_DIR\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1961:             RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1962:             rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1963:             [ \"$RECORD_STATUS\" -eq 0 ] || exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1964:             done <<'DEEP_LOOP_SELFCHECK_ADJUDICATIONS'\n1965:             {selfcheck_adjudications}\n1966:             DEEP_LOOP_SELFCHECK_ADJUDICATIONS\n1967:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\n1968:           on_fail:\n1969:             action: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. An append the gateway rejected leaves the ledger and the registry disagreeing, so the verdict that follows would read a stale count.\"\n1970:             halt: true\n1971:             release_lock: step_release_lock\n1972:           log: \"Adversarial self-check adjudicated {selfcheck_adjudications}; the verdict reads the refreshed registry.\"\n1973: \n1974:       # H-1 verdict derivation: parse findings JSONL, map highest severity to verdict\n1975:       # - PASS: no P0 or P1 findings (P2-only or clean)\n1976:       # - CONDITIONAL: any P1 finding or open search debt (no P0, no failed gate)\n1977:       # - FAIL: any P0 finding, or a required quality gate (evidence, scope, coverage) still failing at the terminal stop\n1978:       # Final line of iteration-NNN.md MUST be exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" / \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" / \"Review verdict: FAIL\"\n1979:       step_derive_verdict:\n1980:         action: \"Derive review verdict from accumulated findings\"\n1981:         note: \"ac_coverage_signal is advisory while the validation rule is INFO/default-off; include it in synthesis traceability, but do not change the exact verdict enum from this signal alone.\"\n1982:         branch_on: \"config.fanout\"\n1983:         if_present:\n1984:           command: |\n1985:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs \\\n1986:               --active-p0 {p0_count} \\\n1987:               --active-p1 {p1_count} \\\n1988:               --active-p2 {p2_count} \\\n1989:               --search-debt {search_debt_count} \\\n1990:               --failed-gate-ids '{failed_required_gate_ids}'\n1991:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1992:           wait_for_completion: true\n1993:           bind_from_output:\n1994:             verdict: \"verdict\"\n1995:             has_advisories: \"has_advisories\"\n1996:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n1997:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n1998:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n1999:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n2000:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. The values the merge bound are the authority on a fan-out root, so an unreadable bound value must stop the run rather than let a verdict be guessed.\"\n2001:         if_absent:\n2002:           command: |\n2003:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs \\\n2004:               --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n2005:               --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n2006:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2007:           wait_for_completion: true\n2008:           bind_from_output:\n2009:             verdict: \"verdict\"\n2010:             has_advisories: \"has_advisories\"\n2011:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n2012:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n2013:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n2014:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n2015:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. A non-zero exit means the registry or the state log could not be read, so this stop has no verdict yet and none may be assumed.\"\n2016:         outputs:\n2017:           - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n2018:           - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n2019:           - active_p0: \"Active P0 count the verdict used\"\n2020:           - active_p1: \"Active P1 count the verdict used\"\n2021:           - active_p2: \"Active P2 count the verdict used\"\n2022:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n2023:         contract: |\n2024:           Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n2025:           Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n2026: \n2027:       step_emit_resource_map:\n2028:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n2029:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n2030:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n2031:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n2032:         read:\n2033:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2034:           - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2035:         write:\n2036:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n2037:         guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n2038:         note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n2039: \n2040:       step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n2041:         action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n2042:         note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n2043: \n2044:       step_compile_review_report:\n2045:         action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n2046:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2047:         instructions: |\n2048:           **Zero-iteration stop:** When {state_paths.state_log} holds no line with type \"iteration\" (on a fan-out root, when none of the lineage state logs under {state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/ holds one), the review did not run, and the report says so instead of reporting on work that never happened:\n2049:              - Executive Summary: open with `Review did not run`, state the stop reason and `0 iterations dispatched`, keep the verdict and hasAdvisories bound by step_derive_verdict unchanged, and state that the P0/P1/P2 counts mean not examined rather than clean.\n2050:              - Planning Trigger: state that `/speckit:plan` is not required, and set the Planning Packet to `triggered: false` and `reviewDidNotRun: true` with `remediationWorkstreams: []`, keeping every other required key from section 2 at an empty value.\n2051:              - Next step: name `/deep:review` again with a duration budget or iteration cap that allows at least one pass.\n2052:              - Sections 3 to 8: give each a single line saying the review did not run.\n2053: \n2054:           Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n2055: \n2056:           1. **Executive Summary**\n2057:              - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n2058:              - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n2059:              - P0/P1/P2 counts: {active_p0}, {active_p1}, {active_p2}, the counts the verdict used, stated as such\n2060:              - Self-check outcomes: each finding the adversarial self-check confirmed, downgraded or called a false positive. On a single-executor run the counts above already reflect them, so list them for reference\n2061:              - Review scope summary\n2062:              - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n2063: \n2064:           2. **Planning Trigger**\n2065:              - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n2066:              - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n2067:              - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n2068:              - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n2069: \n2070:           3. **Active Finding Registry**\n2071:              - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n2072:              - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n2073: \n2074:           4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n2075:              - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n2076: \n2077:           5. **Spec Seed**\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2078]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 1748-2077\n1748:         note: \"Reducer outputs findingsRegistry, dashboardMetrics, and strategyUpdates. Re-running the same inputs must be idempotent.\"\n1749: \n1750:       step_graph_upsert:\n1751:         action: \"Project canonical review coverage plus optional graphEvents into graph nodes and edges, then upsert it\"\n1752:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1753:         read:\n1754:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1755:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1756:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1757:         transform: |\n1758:           1. Read the latest iteration JSONL record after reducer completion.\n1759:           2. Seed one stable DIMENSION node for every configured review dimension, falling back to correctness, security, traceability, and maintainability.\n1760:           3. Seed one stable FILE node for every latest-record filesReviewed entry and emit a COVERS edge from each latest-record dimension to each reviewed file.\n1761:           4. Merge optional graphEvents nodes after normalizing type = uppercase(event.kind || event.nodeKind || event.type); keep only DIMENSION, FILE, FINDING, EVIDENCE, REMEDIATION, BUG_CLASS, INVARIANT, PRODUCER, CONSUMER, TEST.\n1762:           5. Merge optional graphEvents edges after normalizing relation = uppercase(event.relation); keep only COVERS, EVIDENCE_FOR, CONTRADICTS, RESOLVES, CONFIRMS, ESCALATES, IN_DIMENSION, IN_FILE.\n1763:           6. Emit nodes as { id, type, name, iteration, metadata } and edges as { id, relation, sourceId, targetId, metadata }, deduplicated by id.\n1764:           7. Discard malformed or unknown optional events without discarding canonical dimension and file coverage.\n1765:         bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{session_id}\\\" --nodes '{graph_nodes_json}' --edges '{graph_edges_json}'\"\n1766:         note: \"Invoke the runtime script directly. Canonical iteration fields provide baseline coverage; graphEvents add richer evidence.\"\n1767:         outputs:\n1768:           - graph_nodes_json: \"JSON array of canonical and optional review graph nodes\"\n1769:           - graph_edges_json: \"JSON array of canonical and optional review graph edges\"\n1770: \n1771:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Iteration ───\n1772:       gate_post_iteration:\n1773:         applies_to: confirm\n1774:         type: approval_gate\n1775:         purpose: \"Show iteration findings and get approval for next step\"\n1776:         present: |\n1777:           ## Review Iteration {current_iteration} Results\n1778: \n1779:           **Dimensions**: {dimensions}\n1780:           **New Findings**: {findings_count} (P0={severity_counts.P0} P1={severity_counts.P1} P2={severity_counts.P2})\n1781:           **newFindingsRatio**: {newFindingsRatio}\n1782:           **Status**: {status}\n1783:           **Cumulative Findings**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1784:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n1785:           **Traceability**: {traceability_checks.summary}\n1786:           **Stuck Count**: {stuck_count}\n1787: \n1788:           **Recent Iteration Summary**:\n1789:           {last_3_summaries}\n1790: \n1791:           Options:\n1792:           A) Continue to next iteration\n1793:           B) Continue with adjusted focus: [user provides]\n1794:           C) Stop loop and synthesize\n1795:           D) Cancel entirely\n1796:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1797:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1798:         on_A: { proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n1799:         on_B: { action: \"Set next_dimension to user's choice in strategy.md\", proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n1800:         on_C: { set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }, run_first: record_terminal_gates, proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n1801:         on_D: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n1802: \n1803:       step_update_tracking:\n1804:         action: \"Update loop tracking variables\"\n1805:         set:\n1806:           current_iteration: \"{current_iteration + 1}\"\n1807:         log: \"Iteration {N} complete. Dimensions: {dimensions}. newFindingsRatio: {newFindingsRatio}. Findings: P0={severity_counts.P0} P1={severity_counts.P1} P2={severity_counts.P2}.\"\n1808: \n1809:       step_loop_decision:\n1810:         action: \"Return to step_read_state for next iteration\"\n1811:         goto: step_read_state\n1812: \n1813:   # ════════\n1814:   # PHASE 3: SYNTHESIS\n1815:   # ════════\n1816:   phase_synthesis:\n1817:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n1818:     steps:\n1819: \n1820:       step_fanout_merge:\n1821:         description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n1822:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1823:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n1824:         command: |\n1825:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n1826:             --loop-type review \\\n1827:             --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n1828:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1829:         wait_for_completion: true\n1830:         bind_from_output:\n1831:           p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n1832:           p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n1833:           p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n1834:           failed_required_gate_ids: \"failed_required_gate_ids\"\n1835:           search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n1836: \n1837:       step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n1838:         action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n1839:         read:\n1840:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1841:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1842:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1843:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1844:         read_patterns:\n1845:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n1846:         extract:\n1847:           - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count distinct run values (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n1848:           - highest_run: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in those logs in stable lineage order, else 0; otherwise take the highest run value (the integer iteration, else a numeric run) across lines where type === 'iteration' in the root state log, else 0. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n1849:           - current_iteration: \"max(highest_run, iteration_count) + 1\"\n1850:           - p0_count: \"When step_fanout_merge bound it, keep the merged value; the fan-out verdict reads it. Otherwise the count of open findings in {state_paths.findings_registry} with status active and severity P0, for the pre-synthesis display only.\"\n1851:           - p1_count: \"Same rule as p0_count, for severity P1.\"\n1852:           - p2_count: \"Same rule as p0_count, for severity P2.\"\n1853:           - failed_required_gate_ids: \"When step_fanout_merge bound it, keep the merged value. Otherwise take failedRequiredGateIds from the last line of {state_paths.state_log} with type === 'event' and event === 'terminal_gates', else []. Read the state log, not the registry: the reducer last ran before the stop wrote that row.\"\n1854:           - dimensions_covered: \"List of reviewed dimensions\"\n1855:           - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total\"\n1856:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"For spec-folder targets only: if level is 2+ and acceptance-criteria.md exists and implementation-summary.md is in-progress or later, surface the AC_COVERAGE advisory status; otherwise mark exempt.\"\n1857:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records\"\n1858:           - reason: \"Use the latest stop reason if present: read stopReason from the last line of {state_paths.state_log} with type === 'event' and event === 'terminal_gates' when it is newer than the latest stop event, since a manual stop is stored only there; else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused, maxDurationReached.)\"\n1859: \n1860:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Pre-Synthesis ───\n1861:       gate_pre_synthesis:\n1862:         applies_to: confirm\n1863:         type: approval_gate\n1864:         purpose: \"Show all accumulated findings and get approval to synthesize\"\n1865:         present: |\n1866:           ## Review Loop Complete\n1867: \n1868:           **Total Iterations**: {iteration_count}\n1869:           **Stop Reason**: {reason}\n1870:           **Cumulative Findings**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1871:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n1872:           **Recent Iteration Summary**: {last_3_summaries}\n1873: \n1874:           Review the iteration files in `{state_paths.iteration_dir}/` if you want more detail before synthesis.\n1875: \n1876:           Options:\n1877:           A) Proceed to synthesis (compile review/review-report.md)\n1878:           B) Run more iterations (increase max or focus on specific dimension)\n1879:           C) Cancel (keep iteration files)\n1880:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1881:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1882:         on_A: { proceed_to: step_read_all_iterations }\n1883:         on_B: { action: \"Increase max_iterations or adjust focus, return to loop. When reason is maxDurationReached, raise maxDurationMinutes in the config too, or the duration check stops the loop again and writes another terminal record\", proceed_to: phase_loop }\n1884:         on_C: { action: \"Cancel synthesis, keep artifacts\", status: \"PARTIAL\" }\n1885: \n1886:       step_read_all_iterations:\n1887:         action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n1888:         read_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n1889:         read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1890: \n1891:       step_build_finding_registry:\n1892:         action: \"Build deduplicated finding registry from all iterations\"\n1893:         algorithm: |\n1894:           1. Extract all findings from iteration JSONL delta files\n1895:           2. Compute content_hash for each finding (emission requirement):\n1896:              content_hash = sha256(file_path + \"\\u001f\" + line_range + \"\\u001f\" + finding_type + \"\\u001f\" + normalized_description_80chars)\n1897:              Normalized description = whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, first 80 chars of the finding description.\n1898:           3. Two-tier dedup:\n1899:              PRIMARY: group by content_hash field\n1900:                - Same content_hash, multiple dimensions → single finding, merged `dimensions: [<all>]` array\n1901:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n1902:              FALLBACK (legacy records lacking content_hash): file:line + normalized_title\n1903:                - Same file:line, multiple dimensions → single finding, multiple dimension tags\n1904:                - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n1905:           4. Track finding lifecycle:\n1906:              - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n1907:              - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n1908:              - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n1909:           5. Resolve contradictions:\n1910:              - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n1911:              - Determine final severity and status\n1912:           6. Count only 'active' findings for totals. These totals are narrative only: step_derive_verdict reads the registry file after the self-check refreshes it, and the report and the closeout state its counts as the counts the verdict used.\n1913:         outputs:\n1914:           - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n1915: \n1916:       # Adjudication persistence: the Referee's call becomes a claim_adjudication row per\n1917:       # finding, so the registry the verdict reads carries the final severity. A false\n1918:       # positive is recorded as `none`, the scale value for a claim that is not a finding.\n1919:       step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n1920:         action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n1921:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1922:         algorithm: |\n1923:           For each active P0/P1 finding:\n1924:             1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n1925:             2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n1926:             3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n1927:           Record one `<findingId> <finalSeverity>` pair for every call the Referee made\n1928:           here: the severity it settled on, or `none` when it called the finding a false\n1929:           positive. An empty list means the Referee changed nothing.\n1930:           On a single-executor run, append one deep_review.claim_adjudication row per pair\n1931:           through the gateway, then refresh the registry once. The verdict step that\n1932:           follows reads the refreshed registry, so a downgrade or a false positive changes\n1933:           the counts the verdict, the report and the closeout all use.\n1934:           On a fan-out root, record the pairs for the report only: the root has no state\n1935:           log before closeout, and the merged lineage counts are what that verdict reads.\n1936:         extract:\n1937:           - selfcheck_adjudications: \"One `<findingId> <finalSeverity>` pair per line, using the findingId exactly as it appears in openFindings of {state_paths.findings_registry}, empty when the Referee changed nothing\"\n1938:           - adjudication_mode: \"`mode` of the latest claim_adjudication gate row (the newest one without a findingId), else \\\"review\\\"\"\n1939:           - adjudication_run: \"`run` of that gate row, else {highest_run}\"\n1940:           - adjudication_passed: \"`passed` of that gate row, else true\"\n1941:           - adjudication_active_p0_p1: \"`activeP0P1` of that gate row, else {p0_count} plus {p1_count}\"\n1942:           - adjudication_missing_packets: \"`missingPackets` of that gate row as a JSON array, else []\"\n1943:           - adjudication_reason: \"`reason` of that gate row as a JSON value, else \\\"adversarial self-check\\\"\"\n1944:         branch_on: \"config.fanout\"\n1945:         if_present:\n1946:           action: \"Record the pairs in the Executive Summary for reference. Do not append: a fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, and each lineage already adjudicated its own findings, so the merged counts are the authority here.\"\n1947:         if_absent:\n1948:           # The row is staged for the append gateway: the state log is a projection of the\n1949:           # ledger, so a row written beside it is dropped by the next refresh.\n1950:           command: |\n1951:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1952:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1953:             RUN_DIR=\"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\"\n1954:             while read -r FINDING_ID FINAL_SEVERITY; do\n1955:             [ -n \"$FINDING_ID\" ] || continue\n1956:             EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-claim-adjudication.XXXXXX\")\"\n1957:             cat <<DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1958:             {\"stem\":\"deep_review.claim_adjudication\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"{adjudication_mode}\",\"run\":{adjudication_run},\"passed\":{adjudication_passed},\"activeP0P1\":{adjudication_active_p0_p1},\"missingPackets\":{adjudication_missing_packets},\"reason\":{adjudication_reason},\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"findingId\":\"$FINDING_ID\",\"finalSeverity\":\"$FINAL_SEVERITY\"}}\n1959:             DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1960:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$RUN_DIR\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1961:             RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1962:             rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1963:             [ \"$RECORD_STATUS\" -eq 0 ] || exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1964:             done <<'DEEP_LOOP_SELFCHECK_ADJUDICATIONS'\n1965:             {selfcheck_adjudications}\n1966:             DEEP_LOOP_SELFCHECK_ADJUDICATIONS\n1967:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\n1968:           on_fail:\n1969:             action: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. An append the gateway rejected leaves the ledger and the registry disagreeing, so the verdict that follows would read a stale count.\"\n1970:             halt: true\n1971:             release_lock: step_release_lock\n1972:           log: \"Adversarial self-check adjudicated {selfcheck_adjudications}; the verdict reads the refreshed registry.\"\n1973: \n1974:       # H-1 verdict derivation: parse findings JSONL, map highest severity to verdict\n1975:       # - PASS: no P0 or P1 findings (P2-only or clean)\n1976:       # - CONDITIONAL: any P1 finding or open search debt (no P0, no failed gate)\n1977:       # - FAIL: any P0 finding, or a required quality gate (evidence, scope, coverage) still failing at the terminal stop\n1978:       # Final line of iteration-NNN.md MUST be exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" / \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" / \"Review verdict: FAIL\"\n1979:       step_derive_verdict:\n1980:         action: \"Derive review verdict from accumulated findings\"\n1981:         note: \"ac_coverage_signal is advisory while the validation rule is INFO/default-off; include it in synthesis traceability, but do not change the exact verdict enum from this signal alone.\"\n1982:         branch_on: \"config.fanout\"\n1983:         if_present:\n1984:           command: |\n1985:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs \\\n1986:               --active-p0 {p0_count} \\\n1987:               --active-p1 {p1_count} \\\n1988:               --active-p2 {p2_count} \\\n1989:               --search-debt {search_debt_count} \\\n1990:               --failed-gate-ids '{failed_required_gate_ids}'\n1991:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1992:           wait_for_completion: true\n1993:           bind_from_output:\n1994:             verdict: \"verdict\"\n1995:             has_advisories: \"has_advisories\"\n1996:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n1997:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n1998:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n1999:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n2000:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. The values the merge bound are the authority on a fan-out root, so an unreadable bound value must stop the run rather than let a verdict be guessed.\"\n2001:         if_absent:\n2002:           command: |\n2003:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs \\\n2004:               --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n2005:               --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n2006:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2007:           wait_for_completion: true\n2008:           bind_from_output:\n2009:             verdict: \"verdict\"\n2010:             has_advisories: \"has_advisories\"\n2011:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n2012:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n2013:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n2014:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n2015:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. A non-zero exit means the registry or the state log could not be read, so this stop has no verdict yet and none may be assumed.\"\n2016:         outputs:\n2017:           - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n2018:           - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n2019:           - active_p0: \"Active P0 count the verdict used\"\n2020:           - active_p1: \"Active P1 count the verdict used\"\n2021:           - active_p2: \"Active P2 count the verdict used\"\n2022:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n2023:         contract: |\n2024:           Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n2025:           Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n2026: \n2027:       step_emit_resource_map:\n2028:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n2029:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n2030:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n2031:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n2032:         read:\n2033:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2034:           - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2035:         write:\n2036:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n2037:         guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n2038:         note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n2039: \n2040:       step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n2041:         action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n2042:         note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n2043: \n2044:       step_compile_review_report:\n2045:         action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n2046:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2047:         instructions: |\n2048:           **Zero-iteration stop:** When {state_paths.state_log} holds no line with type \"iteration\" (on a fan-out root, when none of the lineage state logs under {state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/ holds one), the review did not run, and the report says so instead of reporting on work that never happened:\n2049:              - Executive Summary: open with `Review did not run`, state the stop reason and `0 iterations dispatched`, keep the verdict and hasAdvisories bound by step_derive_verdict unchanged, and state that the P0/P1/P2 counts mean not examined rather than clean.\n2050:              - Planning Trigger: state that `/speckit:plan` is not required, and set the Planning Packet to `triggered: false` and `reviewDidNotRun: true` with `remediationWorkstreams: []`, keeping every other required key from section 2 at an empty value.\n2051:              - Next step: name `/deep:review` again with a duration budget or iteration cap that allows at least one pass.\n2052:              - Sections 3 to 8: give each a single line saying the review did not run.\n2053: \n2054:           Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n2055: \n2056:           1. **Executive Summary**\n2057:              - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n2058:              - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n2059:              - P0/P1/P2 counts: {active_p0}, {active_p1}, {active_p2}, the counts the verdict used, stated as such\n2060:              - Self-check outcomes: each finding the adversarial self-check confirmed, downgraded or called a false positive. On a single-executor run the counts above already reflect them, so list them for reference\n2061:              - Review scope summary\n2062:              - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n2063: \n2064:           2. **Planning Trigger**\n2065:              - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n2066:              - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n2067:              - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n2068:              - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n2069: \n2070:           3. **Active Finding Registry**\n2071:              - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n2072:              - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n2073: \n2074:           4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n2075:              - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n2076: \n2077:           5. **Spec Seed**\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2078]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":330,\"offset\":1748,\"path\":\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830082989,"end":1794830083423}}}}
