lot|:unattended|--unattended] [--phase-folder=PATH]\"\n.skilled/commands/speckit/implement.md:32:1. Parse `$ARGUMENTS` for `:auto`, `:confirm`, `:autopilot`, `:unattended`, or `--unattended`.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/implement.md:36:5. For `:autopilot`, `:unattended`, or `--unattended`, bind execution mode to `autopilot`; do not alias it to `:auto`.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/implement.md:60:| `:autopilot`, `:unattended`, or `--unattended` | `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-implement.yaml` with `execution_mode` autopilot under the workflow's `unattended_autopilot` block: the operator's `workspace_choice` and branch-preserved failure |\n.skilled/commands/speckit/implement.md:65:`:autopilot`, `:unattended`, and `--unattended` must never end with prose-only failure output.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:3:argument-hint: \"<feature-description> [:auto|:confirm|:autopilot|:unattended|--unattended] [:with-context] [:with-phases] [--level=N]\"\n.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:32:1. Parse `$ARGUMENTS` for `:auto`, `:confirm`, `:autopilot`, `:unattended`, or `--unattended`.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:33:2. Treat `:with-context`, `:with-phases`, `--intake-only`, `--phases`, `--phase-names`, `--phase-folder`, `--spec-folder`, `--level`, `--start-state`, `--repair-mode`, and relationship flags as workflow inputs, not execution modes.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:36:5. For `:autopilot`, `:unattended`, or `--unattended`, bind execution mode to `autopilot`; do not alias it to `:auto`.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:46:| `:with-context` | no value | Loads a context package before planning. |\n.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:47:| `:with-phases` | no value | Decomposes the packet into phase children and plans the first one. |\n.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:69:| `:autopilot`, `:unattended`, or `--unattended` | `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-plan.yaml` with `execution_mode` autopilot under the workflow's `unattended_autopilot` block, with unattended task metadata required |\n.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:74:When planning for `:autopilot`, `:unattended`, or `--unattended`, the workflow's task breakdown step, `step_5_5_task_breakdown`, writes the task rows, and every executable task row in `tasks.md` must carry unattended-ready metadata so later implementation can decide eligibility without asking the user.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:88:If the planner cannot assign one of these fields with at least medium confidence, the unattended terminal result must use `uncertainty_blocked` instead of emitting a prose-only stop.\n.skilled/commands/create/repo-rule.md:39:> **`retire` deletes a file and removes two router rows.** It runs interactively unless the operator wrote the `retire` operation and `:auto` together in the same invocation. An operation inferred as `retire` never runs unattended, however the suffix was set.\n.skilled/commands/create/with-human-voice.md:40:> **`apply` rewrites a file in place.** It runs interactively unless the operator wrote the `apply` operation and `:auto` together in the same invocation. An operation inferred as `apply` never runs unattended, however the suffix was set.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:3:argument-hint: \"<feature-description> [:auto|:confirm|:autopilot|:unattended|--unattended] [:with-research] [:with-context] [:with-phases]\"\n.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:32:1. Parse `$ARGUMENTS` for `:auto`, `:confirm`, `:autopilot`, `:unattended`, or `--unattended`.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:33:2. Treat `:with-research`, `:with-context`, `:with-phases`, `--phases`, `--phase-names`, and `--phase-folder` as workflow inputs, not execution modes.\n.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:36:5. For `:autopilot`, `:unattended`, or `--unattended`, bind execution mode to `autopilot`; do not alias it to `:auto`.\n.skill