{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794831083264,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4448441001V2Bmwae03JUZw9","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","messageID":"msg_1e44465da001LCwnMOCl5BKKdv","type":"tool","id":"call_0bf346be2b5b48a98d584037","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 002\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: `attach-config-7` (fan-out child, session `fanout-attach-config-7-1794829999759-g4q8yp`)\n- Area: `attach-config` per `review/review-scope-7.txt`\n- Dimension: traceability\n- Operator review focus: the reviewer followed `review/review-brief-7.txt` again. This iteration covers the matcher's vocabulary against the command documents and the one-name-per-command surfaces it feeds, which is the traceability half of the `attach-config` area. The scorer and docs areas stay with their lineages. No recorded limit is re-reported.\n- Steer channel: `steer.md` still does not exist.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (comment 203-210, matcher 220-244, call sites 255-263 and 512-515) [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:203]\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (436-470) [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:442]\n- `.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md` (argument-hint and input table, context evidence) [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:3]\n- `.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md` (argument-hint and workflow input table, context evidence) [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:3]\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/review.md` (argument-hint, context evidence) [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/review.md:1]\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` (612-629, 696-699, read-only integration surface owned by `scorer-7`)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The widened suffix vocabulary is not mirrored in the transcript scorer's command parser** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210` -- The matcher now reads a `:with-*` modifier, and a chain of modifiers, as the typed command. The transcript scorer's `commandParts` still removes only a trailing `:(auto|confirm|autopilot|unattended)`, so the same typed text becomes a different command name there and the scored offer is missed.\n   - Finding class: cross-surface contract drift in a measurement path (`traceability`)\n   - Scope proof: the changed line is the widened `MODE_SUFFIX` in this area; the consumer is the named scoring surface, which this lineage reviews only as integration evidence.\n   - Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:612`, `:623`, `:697`\n   - Case: a model prints `COMMAND: /speckit:complete:with-research → started` for a row whose expected command is `/speckit:complete`. `commandParts` produces `speckit:complete:with-research`, `namesCommand` compares it with `speckit:complete`, and the mismatch leaves `offerSeen` false even though the command was typed and attached correctly.\n\n   Reproduction of the scorer's own parser, run outside the repository with the exact source regex and split:\n\n   ```\n   /speckit:complete:auto                 -> {namespace:\"speckit\", name:\"complete\"}                namesExpected=true\n   /speckit:complete:with-research        -> {namespace:\"speckit\", name:\"complete:with-research\"}  namesExpected=false\n   /speckit:complete:auto:with-research   -> {namespace:\"speckit\", name:\"complete:auto:with-research\"} namesExpected=false\n   ```\n\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:612] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:623] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:697]\n\n   Why it is P2 and not P1: the user-facing attach path is correct, and the defect is confined to how stored runs are scored. It becomes load-bearing only when a recorded run types one of the new suffixes, and then it undercounts rather than misroutes.\n\n   Claim adjudication:\n   ```json\n   {\"type\":\"claim\",\"claim\":\"A typed command carrying a :with-* modifier is a different command name for the transcript scorer than for the attach matcher, so a correctly typed chained command is scored as unnamed.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"command-attach.ts:210\",\"command-attach.ts:230\",\"score-command-transcripts.mjs:612\",\"score-command-transcripts.mjs:623\",\"score-command-transcripts.mjs:697\",\"command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:443\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Checked whether commandParts strips every mode suffix before splitting, whether namesCommand compares only the base, and whether the scorer's caller tolerates a longer name. It does not: the exact-equality comparison at line 697 rejects the extra segment.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The divergence may be deliberate if a with-* modifier is treated as command content rather than a suffix. The scorer's own comment calls its pattern the mode suffix, and the command docs classify :with-* as a workflow input on the same command, so a typed command with one is still that command.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P2\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade nothing: P2 is already the lowest active tier. If the scorer never reads a stored run with a :with-* suffix, impact is latent, not absent.\"}\n   ```\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | pass | The accepted vocabulary equals the union of every `argument-hint` suffix under `.skilled/commands`: `:auto` (26 files), `:confirm` (25), `:unattended` (3), `:autopilot` (3), `:with-phases` (2), `:with-context` (2), `:with-research` (1). No documented suffix is refused. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:3] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:3] |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | Phase-parent packet has no `checklist.md`; scope is the five area files. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:1] |\n\nThe sweep covered every `argument-hint:` line under `.skilled/commands` (46 files), so the comparison is against the whole advertised surface, not a sample.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `command-attach.ts` is imported by the scorer's fusion path, and both sides name the same typed command there; the drift above is confined to the transcript parser, not to ranking. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1231]\n- The scorer's `commandParts` is also used for document lookup and confirm-workflow stems, so the same extra segment affects three read paths, not only `namesCommand`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:645]\n- The guard tests pin `/speckit:complete:auto:with-research` as a command for the attach matcher, which is the exact input the scorer still splits differently. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:445]\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The scorer's `MODE_SUFFIX` is anchored at the end, so a chain that ends in `:auto` still parses correctly while the same chain ending in `:with-research` does not. The defect is asymmetric, which is why a single path test on `:auto` would not catch it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:612]\n- The command docs treat `:with-*` as a workflow input, not an execution mode, which is a reason to keep its words in prompt tokenization. That choice is separate from the name-parsing defect and does not excuse it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts:43]\n- This finding is reported against the changed matcher line because the transcript parser belongs to the `scorer-7` area. The scorer owner can fix it in its own file; no code was changed here.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Every documented suffix is accepted, and no extra suffix is accepted beyond the documented union. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210]\n- The negative cases stay refused: an unknown modifier before or after a known one gives no command. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:447]\n- `typedCommandForTop` still gates the command on the leading skill's ownership, so the widened vocabulary cannot carry a command under an unrelated skill. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:261]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A missing documented suffix: the sweep found none; the matcher's set is the complete union. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210]\n- A per-command vocabulary requirement in the spec: no spec requirement narrows the suffix set per command, so the shared set is not a spec contradiction. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:365]\n- Double reporting the previous review's file-extension limit: not repeated; the recorded limit states the behavior and this iteration found no new input that breaks it.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security and maintainability (cross-reference pass)\n- Focus area: the vitest config's environment handling as a trust boundary, then the accuracy of the new module comment and the test coverage the branch adds.\n- Reason: traceability produced one P2 on a measurement surface; the remaining configured dimensions are security and maintainability.\n- Rotation status: correctness and traceability complete; security and maintainability next, in one cross-reference pass because two dimensions remain under a three-iteration cap.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: direct diff read plus source-reproduced probes stay productive; no blocked approaches.\n- Required evidence: an input that crosses the test-environment trust boundary, or a comment claim contradicted by a command document.\n- Recovery note: not in recovery.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 002\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage: `attach-config-7` (fan-out child, session `fanout-attach-config-7-1794829999759-g4q8yp`)\\n- Area: `attach-config` per `review/review-scope-7.txt`\\n- Dimension: traceability\\n- Operator review focus: the reviewer followed `review/review-brief-7.txt` again. This iteration covers the matcher's vocabulary against the command documents and the one-name-per-command surfaces it feeds, which is the traceability half of the `attach-config` area. The scorer and docs areas stay with their lineages. No recorded limit is re-reported.\\n- Steer channel: `steer.md` still does not exist.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (comment 203-210, matcher 220-244, call sites 255-263 and 512-515) [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:203]\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (436-470) [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:442]\\n- `.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md` (argument-hint and input table, context evidence) [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:3]\\n- `.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md` (argument-hint and workflow input table, context evidence) [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:3]\\n- `.skilled/commands/deep/review.md` (argument-hint, context evidence) [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/deep/review.md:1]\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` (612-629, 696-699, read-only integration surface owned by `scorer-7`)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The widened suffix vocabulary is not mirrored in the transcript scorer's command parser** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210` -- The matcher now reads a `:with-*` modifier, and a chain of modifiers, as the typed command. The transcript scorer's `commandParts` still removes only a trailing `:(auto|confirm|autopilot|unattended)`, so the same typed text becomes a different command name there and the scored offer is missed.\\n   - Finding class: cross-surface contract drift in a measurement path (`traceability`)\\n   - Scope proof: the changed line is the widened `MODE_SUFFIX` in this area; the consumer is the named scoring surface, which this lineage reviews only as integration evidence.\\n   - Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:612`, `:623`, `:697`\\n   - Case: a model prints `COMMAND: /speckit:complete:with-research → started` for a row whose expected command is `/speckit:complete`. `commandParts` produces `speckit:complete:with-research`, `namesCommand` compares it with `speckit:complete`, and the mismatch leaves `offerSeen` false even though the command was typed and attached correctly.\\n\\n   Reproduction of the scorer's own parser, run outside the repository with the exact source regex and split:\\n\\n   ```\\n   /speckit:complete:auto                 -> {namespace:\\\"speckit\\\", name:\\\"complete\\\"}                namesExpected=true\\n   /speckit:complete:with-research        -> {namespace:\\\"speckit\\\", name:\\\"complete:with-research\\\"}  namesExpected=false\\n   /speckit:complete:auto:with-research   -> {namespace:\\\"speckit\\\", name:\\\"complete:auto:with-research\\\"} namesExpected=false\\n   ```\\n\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:612] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:623] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:697]\\n\\n   Why it is P2 and not P1: the user-facing attach path is correct, and the defect is confined to how stored runs are scored. It becomes load-bearing only when a recorded run types one of the new suffixes, and then it undercounts rather than misroutes.\\n\\n   Claim adjudication:\\n   ```json\\n   {\\\"type\\\":\\\"claim\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"A typed command carrying a :with-* modifier is a different command name for the transcript scorer than for the attach matcher, so a correctly typed chained command is scored as unnamed.\\\",\\\"evidenceRefs\\\":[\\\"command-attach.ts:210\\\",\\\"command-attach.ts:230\\\",\\\"score-command-transcripts.mjs:612\\\",\\\"score-command-transcripts.mjs:623\\\",\\\"score-command-transcripts.mjs:697\\\",\\\"command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:443\\\"],\\\"counterevidenceSought\\\":\\\"Checked whether commandParts strips every mode suffix before splitting, whether namesCommand compares only the base, and whether the scorer's caller tolerates a longer name. It does not: the exact-equality comparison at line 697 rejects the extra segment.\\\",\\\"alternativeExplanation\\\":\\\"The divergence may be deliberate if a with-* modifier is treated as command content rather than a suffix. The scorer's own comment calls its pattern the mode suffix, and the command docs classify :with-* as a workflow input on the same command, so a typed command with one is still that command.\\\",\\\"finalSeverity\\\":\\\"P2\\\",\\\"confidence\\\":\\\"high\\\",\\\"downgradeTrigger\\\":\\\"Downgrade nothing: P2 is already the lowest active tier. If the scorer never reads a stored run with a :with-* suffix, impact is latent, not absent.\\\"}\\n   ```\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | The accepted vocabulary equals the union of every `argument-hint` suffix under `.skilled/commands`: `:auto` (26 files), `:confirm` (25), `:unattended` (3), `:autopilot` (3), `:with-phases` (2), `:with-context` (2), `:with-research` (1). No documented suffix is refused. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:3] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:3] |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | Phase-parent packet has no `checklist.md`; scope is the five area files. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:1] |\\n\\nThe sweep covered every `argument-hint:` line under `.skilled/commands` (46 files), so the comparison is against the whole advertised surface, not a sample.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `command-attach.ts` is imported by the scorer's fusion path, and both sides name the same typed command there; the drift above is confined to the transcript parser, not to ranking. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1231]\\n- The scorer's `commandParts` is also used for document lookup and confirm-workflow stems, so the same extra segment affects three read paths, not only `namesCommand`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:645]\\n- The guard tests pin `/speckit:complete:auto:with-research` as a command for the attach matcher, which is the exact input the scorer still splits differently. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:445]\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The scorer's `MODE_SUFFIX` is anchored at the end, so a chain that ends in `:auto` still parses correctly while the same chain ending in `:with-research` does not. The defect is asymmetric, which is why a single path test on `:auto` would not catch it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:612]\\n- The command docs treat `:with-*` as a workflow input, not an execution mode, which is a reason to keep its words in prompt tokenization. That choice is separate from the name-parsing defect and does not excuse it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts:43]\\n- This finding is reported against the changed matcher line because the transcript parser belongs to the `scorer-7` area. The scorer owner can fix it in its own file; no code was changed here.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Every documented suffix is accepted, and no extra suffix is accepted beyond the documented union. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210]\\n- The negative cases stay refused: an unknown modifier before or after a known one gives no command. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:447]\\n- `typedCommandForTop` still gates the command on the leading skill's ownership, so the widened vocabulary cannot carry a command under an unrelated skill. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:261]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A missing documented suffix: the sweep found none; the matcher's set is the complete union. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210]\\n- A per-command vocabulary requirement in the spec: no spec requirement narrows the suffix set per command, so the shared set is not a spec contradiction. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:365]\\n- Double reporting the previous review's file-extension limit: not repeated; the recorded limit states the behavior and this iteration found no new input that breaks it.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security and maintainability (cross-reference pass)\\n- Focus area: the vitest config's environment handling as a trust boundary, then the accuracy of the new module comment and the test coverage the branch adds.\\n- Reason: traceability produced one P2 on a measurement surface; the remaining configured dimensions are security and maintainability.\\n- Rotation status: correctness and traceability complete; security and maintainability next, in one cross-reference pass because two dimensions remain under a three-iteration cap.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: direct diff read plus source-reproduced probes stay productive; no blocked approaches.\\n- Required evidence: an input that crosses the test-environment trust boundary, or a comment claim contradicted by a command document.\\n- Recovery note: not in recovery.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794831057985,"end":1794831083264}}}}
