{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794831567710,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","part":{"partID":"prt_1e44c4970001BP7scriG3Q2myg","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeeMt5FpZ1Wzv563","messageID":"msg_1e44c3e7b001Ul1p2m4CQ6RUoj","type":"tool","id":"call_e66dec5b71a2432dad2c0057","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":75,"offset":1090,"path":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs, lines 1090-1164\n1090: function completionFromArtifacts({ lineageDir, lineage, records, loopType }) {\n1091:   if (!lineageDir) return { complete: false, reason: 'no lineage artifact directory to check' };\n1092:   const dir = lineageDir;\n1093: \n1094:   // The terminal report artifact differs by loop type: a research lineage leaves research.md,\n1095:   // a review lineage leaves review-report.md. Research also never emits a review-style\n1096:   // synthesis event (its terminal event is maxIterationsReached), so this artifact check is\n1097:   // the authoritative completion signal for a forced-depth research run.\n1098:   const reportName = loopType === 'research' ? 'research.md' : 'review-report.md';\n1099:   const reportPath = path.join(dir, reportName);\n1100:   if (!fs.existsSync(reportPath)) return { complete: false, reason: `no ${reportName} on disk` };\n1101: \n1102:   const diskNumbers = iterationNumbersOnDisk(dir);\n1103:   const recordCount = records.filter((r) => r && r.type === 'iteration').length;\n1104:   const observed = Math.max(diskNumbers.length, recordCount);\n1105:   if (observed < lineage.iterations) {\n1106:     return { complete: false, reason: `only ${observed} of ${lineage.iterations} iterations on disk` };\n1107:   }\n1108:   const violation = forcedDepthIterationViolation({\n1109:     diskNumbers: diskNumbers.length > 0 ? diskNumbers : null,\n1110:     records,\n1111:     cap: lineage.iterations,\n1112:     stateLogPath: requiredLineageStateLogPath(loopType, dir),\n1113:   });\n1114:   if (violation) return { complete: false, reason: violation };\n1115:   return { complete: true, reason: '' };\n1116: }\n1117: \n1118: function findMaxIterationsPolicyViolation({ loopType, stateRead, lineage, stopPolicy, lineageDir }) {\n1119:   // Forced-depth validation applies to both loop types: stopPolicy=max-iterations means the\n1120:   // lineage must run every iteration and convergence before the cap is telemetry only. The\n1121:   // iteration count is the shared signal, but the terminal completion artifact differs — a\n1122:   // research lineage leaves research.md plus a terminal maxIterationsReached event (no review-\n1123:   // style synthesis event), a review lineage leaves review-report.md — so completion detection\n1124:   // is loop-type-aware below.\n1125:   if ((loopType !== 'review' && loopType !== 'research') || stopPolicy !== 'max-iterations') return null;\n1126:   if (typeof lineage.iterations !== 'number' || lineage.iterations <= 0) {\n1127:     return 'stopPolicy=max-iterations requires a positive lineage iteration cap';\n1128:   }\n1129: \n1130:   const stateFile = lineageStateLogName(loopType) || 'the lineage state log';\n1131:   if (!stateRead || stateRead.missing) {\n1132:     return `missing ${stateFile} for max-iterations stop-policy validation`;\n1133:   }\n1134:   if (stateRead.parseError) {\n1135:     return `could not parse ${stateFile}: ${stateRead.parseError}`;\n1136:   }\n1137: \n1138:   const records = stateRead.records;\n1139:   const iterationCount = records.filter((record) => record && record.type === 'iteration').length;\n1140:   const synthesis = findSynthesisRecord(records);\n1141:   if (!synthesis) {\n1142:     // The event is a self-report, and a producer that did the work can still name\n1143:     // it something the contract never listed — observed across runs of one model\n1144:     // on one prompt: `synthesis_complete`, then `phase_synthesis_complete`, then\n1145:     // `synthesis`. Discarding a finished review over the word it chose destroys\n1146:     // hours of real analysis to enforce a spelling. Fall back to what the lineage\n1147:     // actually left on disk, which is the evidence the event was only claiming.\n1148:     const evidence = completionFromArtifacts({ lineageDir, lineage, records, loopType });\n1149:     if (evidence.complete) return null;\n1150:     return `missing synthesis event and ${evidence.reason} for max-iterations stop-policy validation`;\n1151:   }\n1152: \n1153:   const totalIterations = lineageDir\n1154:     ? countIterationFiles(lineageDir)\n1155:     : iterationCount;\n1156:   if (totalIterations !== lineage.iterations) {\n1157:     return `expected ${lineage.iterations} iterations, got ${totalIterations}`;\n1158:   }\n1159:   const setViolation = forcedDepthIterationViolation({\n1160:     diskNumbers: lineageDir ? iterationNumbersOnDisk(lineageDir) : null,\n1161:     records,\n1162:     cap: lineage.iterations,\n1163:     stateLogPath: stateRead.statePath\n1164:       || (lineageDir ? requiredLineageStateLogPath(loopType, lineageDir) : null),\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1165]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs, lines 1090-1164\n1090: function completionFromArtifacts({ lineageDir, lineage, records, loopType }) {\n1091:   if (!lineageDir) return { complete: false, reason: 'no lineage artifact directory to check' };\n1092:   const dir = lineageDir;\n1093: \n1094:   // The terminal report artifact differs by loop type: a research lineage leaves research.md,\n1095:   // a review lineage leaves review-report.md. Research also never emits a review-style\n1096:   // synthesis event (its terminal event is maxIterationsReached), so this artifact check is\n1097:   // the authoritative completion signal for a forced-depth research run.\n1098:  